      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where the suspect, offender or volunteer is a child or an incapable\nperson, the following people may act as interview friends:\n\n(a) a parent, guardian or other person chosen by, or acceptable\nto, the suspect, offender or volunteer;",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Where the suspect, offender or volunteer is a child or an incapable\nperson, the following people may act as interview friends:\n\n(a) a parent, guardian or other person chosen by, or acceptable\nto, the suspect, offender or volunteer;",
