    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wd-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WD(4) Forensic procedure may be carried out with informed",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wd-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Nothing in this Part or Part IC prevents the carrying out of a\nforensic procedure, with the informed consent of the suspect,\nduring the investigation period provided for by Part IC. However,\nneither carrying out the forensic procedure, nor any delay\nassociated with carrying out the forensic procedure, operates to\nextend the investigation period provided for by Part IC.\nNote:\nBy contrast, the carrying out of a forensic procedure in accordance\nwith a magistrate’s order under Division 5, and associated delays, may\ndelay the expiration of the investigation period provided for by",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Nothing in this Part or Part IC prevents the carrying out of a\nforensic procedure, with the informed consent of the suspect,\nduring the investigation period provided for by Part IC. However,\nneither carrying out the forensic procedure, nor any delay\nassociated with carrying out the forensic procedure, operates to\nextend the investigation period provided for by Part IC.\nNote:\nBy contrast, the carrying out of a forensic procedure in accordance\nwith a magistrate’s order under Division 5, and associated delays, may\ndelay the expiration of the investigation period provided for by",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wd"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wd-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wd-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a31a5cfb8e9fc07fb47104530bb963d3cf12163b0e38a15baae26882aea524d9",
      "skos:note": "Informed consent allows forensic procedure during investigation period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wd-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WD(4) Forensic procedure may be carried out with informed",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Nothing in this Part or Part IC prevents the carrying out of a\nforensic procedure, with the informed consent of the suspect,\nduring the investigation period provided for by Part IC. However,\nneither carrying out the forensic procedure, nor any delay\nassociated with carrying out the forensic procedure, operates to\nextend the investigation period provided for by Part IC.\nNote:\nBy contrast, the carrying out of a forensic procedure in accordance\nwith a magistrate’s order under Division 5, and associated delays, may\ndelay the expiration of the investigation period provided for by"
    },
