    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WK Withdrawal of consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "If a person expressly withdraws consent to the carrying out of a\nforensic procedure under this Part (or if the withdrawal of such\nconsent can reasonably be inferred from the person’s conduct)\nbefore or during the carrying out of the forensic procedure, then:\n\n(a) the forensic procedure is to be treated from the time of the\nwithdrawal as a forensic procedure for which consent has\nbeen refused; and\n\n(b) the forensic procedure is not to proceed except by order of a\nconstable under Division 4 or a magistrate under Division 5.",
      "skos:definition": "If a person expressly withdraws consent to the carrying out of a\nforensic procedure under this Part (or if the withdrawal of such\nconsent can reasonably be inferred from the person’s conduct)\nbefore or during the carrying out of the forensic procedure, then:\n\n(a) the forensic procedure is to be treated from the time of the\nwithdrawal as a forensic procedure for which consent has\nbeen refused; and\n\n(b) the forensic procedure is not to proceed except by order of a\nconstable under Division 4 or a magistrate under Division 5.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wk-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wk-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f9435f80d29c467f67843f497289c332e9e446cfb6c01f92dbc87c000214e743",
      "skos:note": "Forensic procedure cannot proceed without consent after withdrawal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WK Withdrawal of consent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "If a person expressly withdraws consent to the carrying out of a\nforensic procedure under this Part (or if the withdrawal of such\nconsent can reasonably be inferred from the person’s conduct)\nbefore or during the carrying out of the forensic procedure, then:\n\n(a) the forensic procedure is to be treated from the time of the\nwithdrawal as a forensic procedure for which consent has\nbeen refused; and\n\n(b) the forensic procedure is not to proceed except by order of a\nconstable under Division 4 or a magistrate under Division 5."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wk-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wk"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wk-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Cannot proceed",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Consent withdrawn",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Forensic procedure halted"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WL Recording of giving of information and suspect’s responses",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The constable must, if practicable, ensure that the giving of the\ninformation about the proposed forensic procedure and the\nsuspect’s responses (if any) are tape recorded.\n\n(2) If tape recording the giving of the information and the suspect’s\nresponses (if any) is not practicable, the constable must ensure that\na written record of the giving of the information and the suspect’s\nresponses (if any) is made, and that a copy of the record is made\navailable to the suspect.\nNote 1:\nDivision 9 contains provisions about making copies of material\n(including copies of tapes) available to the suspect.\nNote 2:\nIf a foreign law enforcement agency requests that a forensic procedure\nbe carried out on a suspect, a copy of the tape recording or the written\nrecord may also be provided to the foreign law enforcement agency:\nsee subsection 23YQD(2).\n23WLA  Time for carrying out forensic procedure—suspect not in\ncustody\n\n(1) If a suspect who is not in custody:\n\n(a) consents to a forensic procedure; and\n\n(b) presents himself or herself to the investigating constable to\nundergo the procedure;\nthe procedure must be carried out as quickly as reasonably possible\nbut in any case within the following period:\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect is an Aboriginal person or a Torres Strait\nIslander—2 hours after the suspect so presents himself or\nherself;\n\n(d) in any other case—4 hours after the suspect so presents\nhimself or herself.\n\n(2) In working out any period of time for the purposes of\nsubsection (1), the following times are to be disregarded:\n\n(a) the time (if any) that is reasonably required to convey the\nsuspect from the place where the suspect presents himself or\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by consent  Division 3\n\nSection 23WLA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nherself to the investigating constable to the nearest premises\nwhere facilities for carrying out the procedure in accordance\nwith this Part are available to the investigating constable;\n\n(b) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed to allow the suspect, or someone else\non the suspect’s behalf, to communicate with a legal\npractitioner, friend, relative, parent, guardian, interpreter,\nmedical practitioner, dentist or other person as provided by\nthis Part;\n\n(c) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed to allow such a legal practitioner,\nfriend, relative, parent, guardian, interpreter, medical\npractitioner, dentist or other person to arrive at the place\nwhere the procedure is to be carried out;\n\n(d) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed to allow the suspect to receive medical\nattention;\n\n(e) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed because of the suspect’s intoxication;\n\n(f) any reasonable time during which carrying out the procedure\nis suspended or delayed to allow the suspect to rest or\nrecuperate;\n\n(g) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed at the request of the suspect.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The constable must, if practicable, ensure that the giving of the\ninformation about the proposed forensic procedure and the\nsuspect’s responses (if any) are tape recorded.\n\n(2) If tape recording the giving of the information and the suspect’s\nresponses (if any) is not practicable, the constable must ensure that\na written record of the giving of the information and the suspect’s\nresponses (if any) is made, and that a copy of the record is made\navailable to the suspect.\nNote 1:\nDivision 9 contains provisions about making copies of material\n(including copies of tapes) available to the suspect.\nNote 2:\nIf a foreign law enforcement agency requests that a forensic procedure\nbe carried out on a suspect, a copy of the tape recording or the written\nrecord may also be provided to the foreign law enforcement agency:\nsee subsection 23YQD(2).\n23WLA  Time for carrying out forensic procedure—suspect not in\ncustody\n\n(1) If a suspect who is not in custody:\n\n(a) consents to a forensic procedure; and\n\n(b) presents himself or herself to the investigating constable to\nundergo the procedure;\nthe procedure must be carried out as quickly as reasonably possible\nbut in any case within the following period:\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect is an Aboriginal person or a Torres Strait\nIslander—2 hours after the suspect so presents himself or\nherself;\n\n(d) in any other case—4 hours after the suspect so presents\nhimself or herself.\n\n(2) In working out any period of time for the purposes of\nsubsection (1), the following times are to be disregarded:\n\n(a) the time (if any) that is reasonably required to convey the\nsuspect from the place where the suspect presents himself or\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by consent  Division 3\n\nSection 23WLA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nherself to the investigating constable to the nearest premises\nwhere facilities for carrying out the procedure in accordance\nwith",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wl-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wl-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wl-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "914d634e421211c28311851bcc0c598b29ade1c40709478fe60615477135f055"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WL Recording of giving of information and suspect’s responses",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The constable must, if practicable, ensure that the giving of the\ninformation about the proposed forensic procedure and the\nsuspect’s responses (if any) are tape recorded.\n\n(2) If tape recording the giving of the information and the suspect’s\nresponses (if any) is not practicable, the constable must ensure that\na written record of the giving of the information and the suspect’s\nresponses (if any) is made, and that a copy of the record is made\navailable to the suspect.\nNote 1:\nDivision 9 contains provisions about making copies of material\n(including copies of tapes) available to the suspect.\nNote 2:\nIf a foreign law enforcement agency requests that a forensic procedure\nbe carried out on a suspect, a copy of the tape recording or the written\nrecord may also be provided to the foreign law enforcement agency:\nsee subsection 23YQD(2).\n23WLA  Time for carrying out forensic procedure—suspect not in\ncustody\n\n(1) If a suspect who is not in custody:\n\n(a) consents to a forensic procedure; and\n\n(b) presents himself or herself to the investigating constable to\nundergo the procedure;\nthe procedure must be carried out as quickly as reasonably possible\nbut in any case within the following period:\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect is an Aboriginal person or a Torres Strait\nIslander—2 hours after the suspect so presents himself or\nherself;\n\n(d) in any other case—4 hours after the suspect so presents\nhimself or herself.\n\n(2) In working out any period of time for the purposes of\nsubsection (1), the following times are to be disregarded:\n\n(a) the time (if any) that is reasonably required to convey the\nsuspect from the place where the suspect presents himself or\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by consent  Division 3\n\nSection 23WLA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nherself to the investigating constable to the nearest premises\nwhere facilities for carrying out the procedure in accordance\nwith this Part are available to the investigating constable;\n\n(b) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed to allow the suspect, or someone else\non the suspect’s behalf, to communicate with a legal\npractitioner, friend, relative, parent, guardian, interpreter,\nmedical practitioner, dentist or other person as provided by\nthis Part;\n\n(c) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed to allow such a legal practitioner,\nfriend, relative, parent, guardian, interpreter, medical\npractitioner, dentist or other person to arrive at the place\nwhere the procedure is to be carried out;\n\n(d) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed to allow the suspect to receive medical\nattention;\n\n(e) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed because of the suspect’s intoxication;\n\n(f) any reasonable time during which carrying out the procedure\nis suspended or delayed to allow the suspect to rest or\nrecuperate;\n\n(g) any time during which carrying out the procedure is\nsuspended or delayed at the request of the suspect."
    },
