    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wm-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WM(3) Non-intimate forensic procedure may be carried out by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wm-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(3) This Division does not authorise keeping a suspect in custody, in\norder to carry out a forensic procedure, after the expiration of the\ninvestigation period provided for by Part IC.\nNote:\nIf it is necessary to keep a suspect in custody after the expiration of\nthe Part IC investigation period in order to carry out a forensic\nprocedure, an order of a magistrate under Division 5 will have to be\nobtained to authorise this.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) This Division does not authorise keeping a suspect in custody, in\norder to carry out a forensic procedure, after the expiration of the\ninvestigation period provided for by Part IC.\nNote:\nIf it is necessary to keep a suspect in custody after the expiration of\nthe Part IC investigation period in order to carry out a forensic\nprocedure, an order of a magistrate under Division 5 will have to be\nobtained to authorise this.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wm"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wm-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wm-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f37ba3521d10c34b20e6082f53a4fcd890454bffd9c6c086f7d869bbe915773c",
      "skos:note": "Keeping a suspect in custody after investigation period expiration requires magistrate order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wm-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WM(3) Non-intimate forensic procedure may be carried out by",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(3) This Division does not authorise keeping a suspect in custody, in\norder to carry out a forensic procedure, after the expiration of the\ninvestigation period provided for by Part IC.\nNote:\nIf it is necessary to keep a suspect in custody after the expiration of\nthe Part IC investigation period in order to carry out a forensic\nprocedure, an order of a magistrate under Division 5 will have to be\nobtained to authorise this."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wm-ss-3-norm",
