      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Senior police officer must be satisfied about suspect's custody before proceeding.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) The suspect is in the lawful custody of a constable.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the suspect is in the lawful custody of a constable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wo-ss-1-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Senior police officer must be satisfied about offence relevance before proceeding.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the suspect committed a relevant offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...there are reasonable grounds to believe that the suspect committed a relevant offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wo-ss-1-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Senior police officer must be satisfied about evidence relevance before proceeding.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the forensic procedure is likely to produce evidence tending to confirm or disprove...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the forensic procedure is likely to produce evidence tending to confirm or disprove that the suspect committed a relevant offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wo-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WO(2) Matters to be considered by senior police officer before",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wo-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In determining whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure\nwithout consent is justified in all the circumstances, the senior\npolice officer must balance the public interest in obtaining\nevidence tending to confirm or disprove that the suspect committed\nthe offence concerned against the public interest in upholding the\nphysical integrity of the suspect.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In determining whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure\nwithout consent is justified in all the circumstances, the senior\npolice officer must balance the public interest in obtaining\nevidence tending to confirm or disprove that the suspect committed\nthe offence concerned against the public interest in upholding the\nphysical integrity of the suspect.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wo"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wo-ss-2-norm"
