    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wr",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WR Circumstances in which magistrate may order forensic",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wr"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "procedure\n\n(1) A magistrate may, under section 23WS or 23XA, order the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect if:\n\n(a) the suspect is not in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(b) the suspect is in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(c) under section 23WE, the suspect cannot consent to the\nforensic procedure; or\n\n(d) the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal.\n\n(2) However, a magistrate is not authorised to order the carrying out of\na forensic procedure on a suspect if the procedure has been\nrequested by a foreign law enforcement agency.",
      "skos:definition": "procedure\n\n(1) A magistrate may, under section 23WS or 23XA, order the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect if:\n\n(a) the suspect is not in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(b) the suspect is in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(c) under section 23WE, the suspect cannot consent to the\nforensic procedure; or\n\n(d) the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal.\n\n(2) However, a magistrate is not authorised to order the carrying out of\na forensic procedure on a suspect if the procedure has been\nrequested by a foreign law enforcement agency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wr-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wr-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0487c249731a7d9064b8671a7e745fffe250a700a04c9a1ecc8450cb8185e57e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wr",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WR Circumstances in which magistrate may order forensic",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "procedure\n\n(1) A magistrate may, under section 23WS or 23XA, order the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect if:\n\n(a) the suspect is not in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(b) the suspect is in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(c) under section 23WE, the suspect cannot consent to the\nforensic procedure; or\n\n(d) the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal.\n\n(2) However, a magistrate is not authorised to order the carrying out of\na forensic procedure on a suspect if the procedure has been\nrequested by a foreign law enforcement agency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wr-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WR(1) Circumstances in which magistrate may order forensic",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wr-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate may, under section 23WS or 23XA, order the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect if:\n\n(a) the suspect is not in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(b) the suspect is in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(c) under section 23WE, the suspect cannot consent to the\nforensic procedure; or\n\n(d) the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A magistrate may, under section 23WS or 23XA, order the\ncarrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect if:\n\n(a) the suspect is not in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(b) the suspect is in custody and has not consented to the\nforensic procedure (whether or not consent has been sought);\nor\n\n(c) under section 23WE, the suspect cannot consent to the\nforensic procedure; or\n\n(d) the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wr"
