        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "There are reasonable grounds to believe that the suspect committed a relevant offence.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) On the evidence before...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...that there are reasonable grounds to believe..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WT(2) Matters to be considered by magistrate before ordering",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wt-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In determining whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure\nis justified in all the circumstances, the magistrate must:\n\n(a) if the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal—balance the public\ninterest in Australia providing and receiving international\nassistance in criminal matters against the public interest in\nupholding the physical integrity of the suspect; and\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23WT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) in any other case—balance the public interest in obtaining\nevidence tending to confirm or disprove that the suspect\ncommitted the offence concerned against the public interest\nin upholding the physical integrity of the suspect.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In determining whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure\nis justified in all the circumstances, the magistrate must:\n\n(a) if the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal—balance the public\ninterest in Australia providing and receiving international\nassistance in criminal matters against the public interest in\nupholding the physical integrity of the suspect; and\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23WT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) in any other case—balance the public interest in obtaining\nevidence tending to confirm or disprove that the suspect\ncommitted the offence concerned against the public interest\nin upholding the physical integrity of the suspect.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a64b3768a3c48582387e67e2c5a07c8529838c9399758165261b98d6018340f9",
      "skos:note": "Balance public interests when ordering forensic procedures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wt-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WT(2) Matters to be considered by magistrate before ordering",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In determining whether the carrying out of the forensic procedure\nis justified in all the circumstances, the magistrate must:\n\n(a) if the forensic procedure has been requested by a foreign\ncountry or an international tribunal—balance the public\ninterest in Australia providing and receiving international\nassistance in criminal matters against the public interest in\nupholding the physical integrity of the suspect; and\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23WT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) in any other case—balance the public interest in obtaining\nevidence tending to confirm or disprove that the suspect\ncommitted the offence concerned against the public interest\nin upholding the physical integrity of the suspect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Public interest balancing",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) In determining...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the magistrate must:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WT(3) Matters to be considered by magistrate before ordering",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wt-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In balancing those interests, the magistrate must have regard to the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) the seriousness of the circumstances surrounding the\ncommission of the relevant offence and the gravity of the\nrelevant offence;\n\n(b) the degree of the suspect’s alleged participation in the\ncommission of the relevant offence;\n\n(c) the age, physical health and mental health of the suspect, to\nthe extent that they are known to the magistrate or can\nreasonably be discovered by the magistrate (by asking the\nsuspect or otherwise);\n\n(e) if the suspect is a child or an incapable person—the welfare\nof the suspect;\n\n(f) whether there is a less intrusive but reasonably practicable\nway of obtaining evidence tending to confirm or disprove\nthat the suspect committed the relevant offence;\n\n(g) if the suspect gives any reasons for refusing to consent—the\nreasons;\n\n(h) if the suspect is in custody:\n\n(i) the period for which the suspect has already been\ndetained; and\n\n(ii) the reasons for any delay in proposing the carrying out\nof the forensic procedure;\n\n(i) any other matter considered relevant to balancing those\ninterests.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In balancing those interests, the magistrate must have regard to the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) the seriousness of the circumstances surrounding the\ncommission of the relevant offence and the gravity of the\nrelevant offence;\n\n(b) the degree of the suspect’s alleged participation in the\ncommission of the relevant offence;\n\n(c) the age, physical health and mental health of the suspect, to\nthe extent that they are known to the magistrate or can\nreasonably be discovered by the magistrate (by asking the\nsuspect or otherwise);\n\n(e) if the suspect is a child or an incapable person—the welfare\nof the suspect;\n\n(f) whether there is a less intrusive but reasonably practicable\nway of obtaining evidence tending to confirm or disprove\nthat the suspect committed the relevant offence;\n\n(g) if the suspect gives any reasons for refusing to consent—the\nreasons;\n\n(h) if the suspect is in custody:\n\n(i) the period for which the suspect has already been\ndetained; and\n\n(ii) the reasons for any delay in proposing the carrying out\nof the forensic procedure;\n\n(i) any other matter considered relevant to balancing those\ninterests.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8ecd6678170ab8b25ed3a6f0eba7a0ff9929f0a99e0b3a4057037d3736504ee9",
      "skos:note": "Consider matters before ordering a forensic procedure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wt-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WT(3) Matters to be considered by magistrate before ordering",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In balancing those interests, the magistrate must have regard to the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) the seriousness of the circumstances surrounding the\ncommission of the relevant offence and the gravity of the\nrelevant offence;\n\n(b) the degree of the suspect’s alleged participation in the\ncommission of the relevant offence;\n\n(c) the age, physical health and mental health of the suspect, to\nthe extent that they are known to the magistrate or can\nreasonably be discovered by the magistrate (by asking the\nsuspect or otherwise);\n\n(e) if the suspect is a child or an incapable person—the welfare\nof the suspect;\n\n(f) whether there is a less intrusive but reasonably practicable\nway of obtaining evidence tending to confirm or disprove\nthat the suspect committed the relevant offence;\n\n(g) if the suspect gives any reasons for refusing to consent—the\nreasons;\n\n(h) if the suspect is in custody:\n\n(i) the period for which the suspect has already been\ndetained; and\n\n(ii) the reasons for any delay in proposing the carrying out\nof the forensic procedure;\n\n(i) any other matter considered relevant to balancing those\ninterests."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wt-ss-3-norm",
