    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wv",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WV Securing the presence of suspect at hearing—suspect in",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wv"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "custody\n\n(1) If the suspect is in the custody of another constable or is otherwise\ndetained under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\n(original custody), the magistrate may, on the application of a\nconstable, issue a warrant directing the person holding the suspect\nin original custody to deliver the suspect into the custody of the\nconstable (temporary custody) for the hearing of an application for\nan order under this Division.\n\n(2) The constable given temporary custody must return the suspect to\nthe place of original custody:\n\n(a) if the application for the order is refused—without delay; or\n\n(b) if the order is made—without delay at the end of the period\nfor which the suspect may be detained in custody under\nsection 23XGD.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23WW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "custody\n\n(1) If the suspect is in the custody of another constable or is otherwise\ndetained under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\n(original custody), the magistrate may, on the application of a\nconstable, issue a warrant directing the person holding the suspect\nin original custody to deliver the suspect into the custody of the\nconstable (temporary custody) for the hearing of an application for\nan order under this Division.\n\n(2) The constable given temporary custody must return the suspect to\nthe place of original custody:\n\n(a) if the application for the order is refused—without delay; or\n\n(b) if the order is made—without delay at the end of the period\nfor which the suspect may be detained in custody under\nsection 23XGD.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23WW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wv-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wv-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21a7f61c15cef4ddedae076d6b7393f1d3d4a9b5c870df60ca0c59b195ef1602"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wv",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WV Securing the presence of suspect at hearing—suspect in",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "custody\n\n(1) If the suspect is in the custody of another constable or is otherwise\ndetained under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\n(original custody), the magistrate may, on the application of a\nconstable, issue a warrant directing the person holding the suspect\nin original custody to deliver the suspect into the custody of the\nconstable (temporary custody) for the hearing of an application for\nan order under this Division.\n\n(2) The constable given temporary custody must return the suspect to\nthe place of original custody:\n\n(a) if the application for the order is refused—without delay; or\n\n(b) if the order is made—without delay at the end of the period\nfor which the suspect may be detained in custody under\nsection 23XGD.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23WW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
