    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wy",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23WY Making of order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wy"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a magistrate makes an order for the carrying out of a forensic\nprocedure, the magistrate must:\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23XA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) give reasons for making the order; and\n\n(b) ensure that a written record of the order is kept; and\n\n(c) order the suspect to attend for the carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure; and\n\n(d) inform the suspect that reasonable force may be used to\nensure that he or she complies with the order for the carrying\nout of the forensic procedure.\n\n(2) The magistrate may give directions as to the time, place and\nmanner in which the procedure is to be carried out.\nSubdivision C—Interim orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a magistrate makes an order for the carrying out of a forensic\nprocedure, the magistrate must:\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23XA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) give reasons for making the order; and\n\n(b) ensure that a written record of the order is kept; and\n\n(c) order the suspect to attend for the carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure; and\n\n(d) inform the suspect that reasonable force may be used to\nensure that he or she complies with the order for the carrying\nout of the forensic procedure.\n\n(2) The magistrate may give directions as to the time, place and\nmanner in which the procedure is to be carried out.\nSubdivision C—Interim orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wy-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23wy-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "48722e67ab5337f408aed2d98a9078e2f0f2950b597f02e1fdb8b7b95e9605f8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wy",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WY Making of order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a magistrate makes an order for the carrying out of a forensic\nprocedure, the magistrate must:\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23XA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) give reasons for making the order; and\n\n(b) ensure that a written record of the order is kept; and\n\n(c) order the suspect to attend for the carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure; and\n\n(d) inform the suspect that reasonable force may be used to\nensure that he or she complies with the order for the carrying\nout of the forensic procedure.\n\n(2) The magistrate may give directions as to the time, place and\nmanner in which the procedure is to be carried out.\nSubdivision C—Interim orders"
    },
