    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23wy-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23WY(1) Making of order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a magistrate makes an order for the carrying out of a forensic\nprocedure, the magistrate must:\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23XA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) give reasons for making the order; and\n\n(b) ensure that a written record of the order is kept; and\n\n(c) order the suspect to attend for the carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure; and\n\n(d) inform the suspect that reasonable force may be used to\nensure that he or she complies with the order for the carrying\nout of the forensic procedure."
    },
