    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XA Interim order for carrying out of a forensic procedure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate may make an interim order authorising the carrying\nout of a forensic procedure on a suspect that must be carried out\nwithout delay if:\n\n(a) subsection 23WR(1) applies; and\n\n(b) the magistrate is satisfied that the probative value of evidence\nobtained as a result of the forensic procedure concerned is\nlikely to be lost or destroyed if there is delay in carrying out\nthe procedure; and\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that there is sufficient evidence to\nindicate that a magistrate is reasonably likely to be satisfied\nof the existence of the matters referred to in\nsubsection 23WT(1) when the application is finally\ndetermined.\n\n(2) An interim order operates as provided by this Subdivision until a\nmagistrate, at a hearing held under Subdivision B, confirms the\ninterim order or disallows the interim order.\nNote:\nSubsection 23XD(2) requires that an interim order specify the\nintended date, time and place of the later hearing.\n\n(3) Subdivision B applies in relation to an order confirming the interim\norder in the same way it applies in relation to an order under",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A magistrate may make an interim order authorising the carrying\nout of a forensic procedure on a suspect that must be carried out\nwithout delay if:\n\n(a) subsection 23WR(1) applies; and\n\n(b) the magistrate is satisfied that the probative value of evidence\nobtained as a result of the forensic procedure concerned is\nlikely to be lost or destroyed if there is delay in carrying out\nthe procedure; and\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that there is sufficient evidence to\nindicate that a magistrate is reasonably likely to be satisfied\nof the existence of the matters referred to in\nsubsection 23WT(1) when the application is finally\ndetermined.\n\n(2) An interim order operates as provided by this Subdivision until a\nmagistrate, at a hearing held under Subdivision B, confirms the\ninterim order or disallows the interim order.\nNote:\nSubsection 23XD(2) requires that an interim order specify the\nintended date, time and place of the later hearing.\n\n(3) Subdivision B applies in relation to an order confirming the interim\norder in the same way it applies in relation to an order under",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xa-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eaa6a4049575606468c8b479d850c3d1c767bd391a1a44807375572147952e9a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XA Interim order for carrying out of a forensic procedure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate may make an interim order authorising the carrying\nout of a forensic procedure on a suspect that must be carried out\nwithout delay if:\n\n(a) subsection 23WR(1) applies; and\n\n(b) the magistrate is satisfied that the probative value of evidence\nobtained as a result of the forensic procedure concerned is\nlikely to be lost or destroyed if there is delay in carrying out\nthe procedure; and\n\n(c) the magistrate is satisfied that there is sufficient evidence to\nindicate that a magistrate is reasonably likely to be satisfied\nof the existence of the matters referred to in\nsubsection 23WT(1) when the application is finally\ndetermined.\n\n(2) An interim order operates as provided by this Subdivision until a\nmagistrate, at a hearing held under Subdivision B, confirms the\ninterim order or disallows the interim order.\nNote:\nSubsection 23XD(2) requires that an interim order specify the\nintended date, time and place of the later hearing.\n\n(3) Subdivision B applies in relation to an order confirming the interim\norder in the same way it applies in relation to an order under"
    },
