    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XC Procedure at hearing of application for interim order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the application is made in person, or by telephone or radio or\nother form of oral communication, the magistrate must ensure that:\n\n(a) the suspect; and\n\n(b) the suspect’s legal representative, if any; and\n\n(c) the suspect’s interview friend, if any;\nare given an opportunity to speak to the magistrate.\n\n(2) If the application is made by telex, fax or other form of written\ncommunication, the magistrate must ensure that:\n\n(a) the suspect; and\n\n(b) the suspect’s legal representative, if any; and\n\n(c) the suspect’s interview friend, if any;\nare given an opportunity to make a written submission to\naccompany the application, or to speak to the magistrate by\ntelephone, radio or other form of oral communication.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the application is made in person, or by telephone or radio or\nother form of oral communication, the magistrate must ensure that:\n\n(a) the suspect; and\n\n(b) the suspect’s legal representative, if any; and\n\n(c) the suspect’s interview friend, if any;\nare given an opportunity to speak to the magistrate.\n\n(2) If the application is made by telex, fax or other form of written\ncommunication, the magistrate must ensure that:\n\n(a) the suspect; and\n\n(b) the suspect’s legal representative, if any; and\n\n(c) the suspect’s interview friend, if any;\nare given an opportunity to make a written submission to\naccompany the application, or to speak to the magistrate by\ntelephone, radio or other form of oral communication.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xc-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2ab0c731ac5e556ff26e5629022920644a689317078bc1d37cf95ec7c471a22b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XC Procedure at hearing of application for interim order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the application is made in person, or by telephone or radio or\nother form of oral communication, the magistrate must ensure that:\n\n(a) the suspect; and\n\n(b) the suspect’s legal representative, if any; and\n\n(c) the suspect’s interview friend, if any;\nare given an opportunity to speak to the magistrate.\n\n(2) If the application is made by telex, fax or other form of written\ncommunication, the magistrate must ensure that:\n\n(a) the suspect; and\n\n(b) the suspect’s legal representative, if any; and\n\n(c) the suspect’s interview friend, if any;\nare given an opportunity to make a written submission to\naccompany the application, or to speak to the magistrate by\ntelephone, radio or other form of oral communication."
    },
