      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate who makes an interim order must inform the\napplicant for the order personally, or by telephone, radio, telex, fax\nor other means of transmission:\n\n(a) that the order has been made; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A magistrate who makes an interim order must inform the\napplicant for the order personally, or by telephone, radio, telex, fax\nor other means of transmission:\n\n(a) that the order has been made; and",
