    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xe",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XE Records of application and interim order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xe"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for an interim order must, at the time of, or as soon\nas practicable after, applying for the interim order, make a record\n(the applicant’s record) of:\n\n(a) the application; and\n\n(b) the grounds for seeking the order; and\n\n(c) the order made; and\n\n(d) the date and time when the order was made; and\n\n(e) the magistrate’s name;\nand sign the record.\n\n(2) The applicant must send a copy of the applicant’s record to the\nmagistrate as soon as practicable after it is made.\n\n(3) The magistrate must, at the time of, or as soon as practicable after,\nmaking an interim order, make a record (the magistrate’s record)\nof:\n\n(a) the application; and\n\n(b) the grounds for seeking the order; and\n\n(c) the order made; and\n\n(d) the date and time when the order was made; and\n\n(e) the reasons for making it;\nand sign the record.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23XF\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The magistrate must send a copy of the magistrate’s record to the\napplicant as soon as practicable after the record is made.\n\n(5) The applicant must ensure that a copy of the magistrate’s record\nand a copy of the applicant’s record are made available to the\nsuspect as soon as practicable after the applicant receives the\nmagistrate’s record.\n\n(6) If the applicant’s record does not, in all material respects, accord\nwith the magistrate’s record, the order is taken to have had no\neffect.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The applicant for an interim order must, at the time of, or as soon\nas practicable after, applying for the interim order, make a record\n(the applicant’s record) of:\n\n(a) the application; and\n\n(b) the grounds for seeking the order; and\n\n(c) the order made; and\n\n(d) the date and time when the order was made; and\n\n(e) the magistrate’s name;\nand sign the record.\n\n(2) The applicant must send a copy of the applicant’s record to the\nmagistrate as soon as practicable after it is made.\n\n(3) The magistrate must, at the time of, or as soon as practicable after,\nmaking an interim order, make a record (the magistrate’s record)\nof:\n\n(a) the application; and\n\n(b) the grounds for seeking the order; and\n\n(c) the order made; and\n\n(d) the date and time when the order was made; and\n\n(e) the reasons for making it;\nand sign the record.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23XF\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The magistrate must send a copy of the magistrate’s record to the\napplicant as soon as practicable after the record is made.\n\n(5) The applicant must ensure that a copy of the magistrate’s record\nand a copy of the applicant’s record are made available to the\nsuspect as soon as practicable after the applicant receives the\nmagistrate’s record.\n\n(6) If the applicant’s record does not, in all material respects, accord\nwith the magistrate’s record, the order is taken to have had no\neffect.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xe-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xe-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xe-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xe-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xe-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xe-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7eba051d92dbad74fb3521dad231877149cc606c68cf1f621759a19d2ebe14c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xe",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XE Records of application and interim order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for an interim order must, at the time of, or as soon\nas practicable after, applying for the interim order, make a record\n(the applicant’s record) of:\n\n(a) the application; and\n\n(b) the grounds for seeking the order; and\n\n(c) the order made; and\n\n(d) the date and time when the order was made; and\n\n(e) the magistrate’s name;\nand sign the record.\n\n(2) The applicant must send a copy of the applicant’s record to the\nmagistrate as soon as practicable after it is made.\n\n(3) The magistrate must, at the time of, or as soon as practicable after,\nmaking an interim order, make a record (the magistrate’s record)\nof:\n\n(a) the application; and\n\n(b) the grounds for seeking the order; and\n\n(c) the order made; and\n\n(d) the date and time when the order was made; and\n\n(e) the reasons for making it;\nand sign the record.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nForensic procedures on suspect by order of a magistrate  Division 5\n\nSection 23XF\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(4) The magistrate must send a copy of the magistrate’s record to the\napplicant as soon as practicable after the record is made.\n\n(5) The applicant must ensure that a copy of the magistrate’s record\nand a copy of the applicant’s record are made available to the\nsuspect as soon as practicable after the applicant receives the\nmagistrate’s record.\n\n(6) If the applicant’s record does not, in all material respects, accord\nwith the magistrate’s record, the order is taken to have had no\neffect."
    },
