    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XF Suspect may be prevented from destroying or contaminating",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "evidence\n\n(1) A constable may, while waiting for the application seeking an\ninterim order to be determined, use reasonable force to prevent the\nsuspect destroying or contaminating any evidence that might be\nobtained by carrying out the forensic procedure if the order is\nmade.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section authorises any person to carry out a forensic\nprocedure before an interim order is made.",
      "skos:definition": "evidence\n\n(1) A constable may, while waiting for the application seeking an\ninterim order to be determined, use reasonable force to prevent the\nsuspect destroying or contaminating any evidence that might be\nobtained by carrying out the forensic procedure if the order is\nmade.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section authorises any person to carry out a forensic\nprocedure before an interim order is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xf-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee8250fb76e094b34b471f13a73dbbe51d1ae142e9df59d7c0d31ec20f0a0a8e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XF Suspect may be prevented from destroying or contaminating",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 57,
      "values:originalText": "evidence\n\n(1) A constable may, while waiting for the application seeking an\ninterim order to be determined, use reasonable force to prevent the\nsuspect destroying or contaminating any evidence that might be\nobtained by carrying out the forensic procedure if the order is\nmade.\n\n(2) Nothing in this section authorises any person to carry out a forensic\nprocedure before an interim order is made."
    },
