      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.57",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A sample taken under an interim order must not be analysed\nunless:\n\n(a) the sample is likely to perish before a final order is made; or\n\n(b) a final order is made.\n\n(2) A person who conducts an analysis in the circumstances set out in\nparagraph (1)(a) must not intentionally disclose the results of the\nanalysis to any person:\n\n(a) during the period before a final order is made; or\n\n(b) if the interim order is disallowed.\nPenalty for a contravention of subsection (2):\nImprisonment\nfor 12 months.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A sample taken under an interim order must not be analysed\nunless:\n\n(a) the sample is likely to perish before a final order is made; or\n\n(b) a final order is made.\n\n(2) A person who conducts an analysis in the circumstances set out in\nparagraph (1)(a) must not intentionally disclose the results of the\nanalysis to any person:\n\n(a) during the period before a final order is made; or\n\n(b) if the interim order is disallowed.\nPenalty for a contravention of subsection (2):\nImprisonment\nfor 12 months.",
