    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xp-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XP(2) Medical practitioner or dentist of suspect’s choice may be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xp-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The expert chosen is to be present at the forensic procedure unless\nhe or she:\n\n(a) is unable, or does not wish, to attend; or\n\n(b) cannot be contacted;\nwithin a reasonable time or, if relevant, within the time in which\nthe person responsible for the effective carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure considers the forensic procedure should be carried out if\nit is to be effective in affording evidence of the relevant offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The expert chosen is to be present at the forensic procedure unless\nhe or she:\n\n(a) is unable, or does not wish, to attend; or\n\n(b) cannot be contacted;\nwithin a reasonable time or, if relevant, within the time in which\nthe person responsible for the effective carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure considers the forensic procedure should be carried out if\nit is to be effective in affording evidence of the relevant offence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xp"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xp-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xp-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "79a12fa656862b4e64d0484768b85f4197d547a637df4311e1eb07e80aad0c8d",
      "skos:note": "Expert chosen may not be required to attend forensic procedure under certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xp-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XP(2) Medical practitioner or dentist of suspect’s choice may be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The expert chosen is to be present at the forensic procedure unless\nhe or she:\n\n(a) is unable, or does not wish, to attend; or\n\n(b) cannot be contacted;\nwithin a reasonable time or, if relevant, within the time in which\nthe person responsible for the effective carrying out of the forensic\nprocedure considers the forensic procedure should be carried out if\nit is to be effective in affording evidence of the relevant offence."
    },
