    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XQ Presence of interview friend or legal representative—children",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "and incapable persons\n\n(1) This section applies if the suspect is:\n\n(a) a child; or\n\n(b) an incapable person.\n\n(2) Either an interview friend or a legal representative (if he or she is\nnot the interview friend) of the suspect must be present while the\nforensic procedure is carried out. Both an interview friend and a\nlegal representative may be present.\n\n(3) An interview friend (other than a legal representative) of the\nsuspect may be excluded from the place where the forensic\nprocedure is being carried out if the interview friend unreasonably\ninterferes with or obstructs the carrying out of the procedure.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nCarrying out forensic procedures on suspects  Division 6\n\nSection 23XR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "and incapable persons\n\n(1) This section applies if the suspect is:\n\n(a) a child; or\n\n(b) an incapable person.\n\n(2) Either an interview friend or a legal representative (if he or she is\nnot the interview friend) of the suspect must be present while the\nforensic procedure is carried out. Both an interview friend and a\nlegal representative may be present.\n\n(3) An interview friend (other than a legal representative) of the\nsuspect may be excluded from the place where the forensic\nprocedure is being carried out if the interview friend unreasonably\ninterferes with or obstructs the carrying out of the procedure.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nCarrying out forensic procedures on suspects  Division 6\n\nSection 23XR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xq-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xq-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "27cadb0c7e3c6508e4ca595d6bc80d8c0a31c13886ffcb8847b5432e0e866fdd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XQ Presence of interview friend or legal representative—children",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "and incapable persons\n\n(1) This section applies if the suspect is:\n\n(a) a child; or\n\n(b) an incapable person.\n\n(2) Either an interview friend or a legal representative (if he or she is\nnot the interview friend) of the suspect must be present while the\nforensic procedure is carried out. Both an interview friend and a\nlegal representative may be present.\n\n(3) An interview friend (other than a legal representative) of the\nsuspect may be excluded from the place where the forensic\nprocedure is being carried out if the interview friend unreasonably\ninterferes with or obstructs the carrying out of the procedure.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nCarrying out forensic procedures on suspects  Division 6\n\nSection 23XR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
