      "values:originalText": "(3) Subsection (2) does not apply if:\n\n(a) the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat, having regard to the suspect’s level of education and\nunderstanding, the suspect is not at a disadvantage in respect\nof the carrying out of the forensic procedure by comparison\nwith members of the Australian community generally; or\n\n(b) the suspect expressly and voluntarily waives his or her right\nto have an interview friend present.\nNote:\nSection 23YK relates to proving a waiver under subsection (3)."
    },
