    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XU Samples—sufficient material to share",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a sample is taken from a suspect under this Part; and\n\n(b) the suspect requests the investigating constable that the\nsample be shared; and\n\n(c) there is sufficient material to be analysed both in the\ninvestigation of the offence and on behalf of the suspect.\n\n(2) The investigating constable must invite the suspect to nominate an\naccredited laboratory to which a part of the material sufficient for\nanalysis will be provided on behalf of the suspect.\n\n(3) If the suspect nominates an accredited laboratory, the investigating\nconstable must ensure that:\n\n(a) a part of the material sufficient for analysis is provided to\nthat laboratory, on behalf of the suspect, within the period of\n28 days beginning on the day of the nomination; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a sample is taken from a suspect under this Part; and\n\n(b) the suspect requests the investigating constable that the\nsample be shared; and\n\n(c) there is sufficient material to be analysed both in the\ninvestigation of the offence and on behalf of the suspect.\n\n(2) The investigating constable must invite the suspect to nominate an\naccredited laboratory to which a part of the material sufficient for\nanalysis will be provided on behalf of the suspect.\n\n(3) If the suspect nominates an accredited laboratory, the investigating\nconstable must ensure that:\n\n(a) a part of the material sufficient for analysis is provided to\nthat laboratory, on behalf of the suspect, within the period of\n28 days beginning on the day of the nomination; and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xu-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xu-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xu-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "07d113006f438a3a8edd7dbccfbc4297a4b9fa432dd18c061356013688465096"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xu",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XU Samples—sufficient material to share",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a sample is taken from a suspect under this Part; and\n\n(b) the suspect requests the investigating constable that the\nsample be shared; and\n\n(c) there is sufficient material to be analysed both in the\ninvestigation of the offence and on behalf of the suspect.\n\n(2) The investigating constable must invite the suspect to nominate an\naccredited laboratory to which a part of the material sufficient for\nanalysis will be provided on behalf of the suspect.\n\n(3) If the suspect nominates an accredited laboratory, the investigating\nconstable must ensure that:\n\n(a) a part of the material sufficient for analysis is provided to\nthat laboratory, on behalf of the suspect, within the period of\n28 days beginning on the day of the nomination; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xu-ss-1",
