    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xx-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits the use of evidence from improper forensic procedures.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) This section applies to:\n\n(a) evidence of forensic material, or evidence consisting of\nforensic material, taken from the person by the forensic\nprocedure;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xx-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on those who would use such evidence.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) This section applies to:\n\n(a) evidence of forensic material, or evidence consisting of\nforensic material, taken from the person by the forensic\nprocedure;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xy",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XY Inadmissibility of evidence where forensic material required",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xy"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "to be destroyed\n\n(1) If a provision of this Part requires forensic material taken from a\nperson by a forensic procedure to be destroyed, subsection (2)\napplies to:\n\n(a) evidence of the forensic material; and\n\n(b) if the material has not been destroyed—evidence consisting\nof the forensic material; and\n\n(c) any results of the analysis of the forensic material; and\n\n(d) any other evidence made or obtained as a result of or in\nconnection with the carrying out of the forensic procedure.\n\n(2) The results of the analysis, and the other evidence, are not\nadmissible if adduced by the prosecution in any proceedings\nagainst the person, but may be admissible if adduced in such\nproceedings by the person.\nSubdivision B—Other evidence",
      "skos:definition": "to be destroyed\n\n(1) If a provision of this Part requires forensic material taken from a\nperson by a forensic procedure to be destroyed, subsection (2)\napplies to:\n\n(a) evidence of the forensic material; and\n\n(b) if the material has not been destroyed—evidence consisting\nof the forensic material; and\n\n(c) any results of the analysis of the forensic material; and\n\n(d) any other evidence made or obtained as a result of or in\nconnection with the carrying out of the forensic procedure.\n\n(2) The results of the analysis, and the other evidence, are not\nadmissible if adduced by the prosecution in any proceedings\nagainst the person, but may be admissible if adduced in such\nproceedings by the person.\nSubdivision B—Other evidence",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xy-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xy-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f5ccc4788aa51b8eb502e3adba2381ec6eb3f91aff0ae8a4f428dbdb23b44725"
    },
    {
