    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xz",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23XZ Admissibility of evidence relating to consent to forensic",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xz"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "procedure\n\nEvidence of a person’s refusal or failure to consent, or withdrawal\nof consent, to a forensic procedure is not admissible in proceedings\nagainst the person except to establish or rebut an allegation that a\nconstable or another person investigating the commission of the\noffence concerned acted contrary to law in carrying out that\ninvestigation.",
      "skos:definition": "procedure\n\nEvidence of a person’s refusal or failure to consent, or withdrawal\nof consent, to a forensic procedure is not admissible in proceedings\nagainst the person except to establish or rebut an allegation that a\nconstable or another person investigating the commission of the\noffence concerned acted contrary to law in carrying out that\ninvestigation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xz-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b018948d71bcfa11b58faef1ec10397f7538eae414a344f471b6749da67790c6",
      "skos:note": "Evidence of refusal or withdrawal of consent is not admissible in proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23xz",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23XZ Admissibility of evidence relating to consent to forensic",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 99,
      "values:originalText": "procedure\n\nEvidence of a person’s refusal or failure to consent, or withdrawal\nof consent, to a forensic procedure is not admissible in proceedings\nagainst the person except to establish or rebut an allegation that a\nconstable or another person investigating the commission of the\noffence concerned acted contrary to law in carrying out that\ninvestigation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xz-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23xz"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ya",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YA Admissibility of evidence relating to carrying out of forensic",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23ya"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "procedure\n\nIn spite of subsection 23XX(4), evidence of how a forensic\nprocedure was carried out is admissible in proceedings against the\nperson in a court:\n\n(a) to establish or rebut an allegation that unreasonable force was\nused to enable the procedure to be carried out; or\n\n(b) to determine the admissibility of a confession or admission or\nother evidence adverse to the person where the person alleges\nthat the evidence was induced or obtained by the use of\nunreasonable force; or\n\n(c) to establish or rebut an allegation that the forensic procedure\nwas not carried out in accordance with Division 6.",
      "skos:definition": "procedure\n\nIn spite of subsection 23XX(4), evidence of how a forensic\nprocedure was carried out is admissible in proceedings against the\nperson in a court:\n\n(a) to establish or rebut an allegation that unreasonable force was\nused to enable the procedure to be carried out; or\n\n(b) to determine the admissibility of a confession or admission or\nother evidence adverse to the person where the person alleges\nthat the evidence was induced or obtained by the use of\nunreasonable force; or\n\n(c) to establish or rebut an allegation that the forensic procedure\nwas not carried out in accordance with Division 6.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ya-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ya-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "499f8686c7b3837f206ff73b485a50bb99f9d2532508da2682cad07cdb891217",
      "skos:note": "Evidence of forensic procedure admissibility in court proceedings"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23ya",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YA Admissibility of evidence relating to carrying out of forensic",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "procedure\n\nIn spite of subsection 23XX(4), evidence of how a forensic\nprocedure was carried out is admissible in proceedings against the\nperson in a court:\n\n(a) to establish or rebut an allegation that unreasonable force was\nused to enable the procedure to be carried out; or\n\n(b) to determine the admissibility of a confession or admission or\nother evidence adverse to the person where the person alleges\nthat the evidence was induced or obtained by the use of\nunreasonable force; or\n\n(c) to establish or rebut an allegation that the forensic procedure\nwas not carried out in accordance with Division 6."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ya-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
