      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ya-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "admission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establishes admissibility of evidence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "None",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Evidence is admissible"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YB Obstructing the carrying out of forensic procedure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies where a constable or magistrate has ordered\nthe carrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect under this\nPart.\n\n(2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), evidence that the suspect:\n\n(a) refused to comply with any reasonable direction in\nconnection with the carrying out of the forensic procedure; or\n\n(b) obstructed, resisted, hindered, used violence against,\nthreatened or intimidated a person in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure;\nis admissible in any proceedings against the suspect in respect of a\nrelevant offence.\n\n(3) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible if the\nforensic procedure was in fact carried out satisfactorily.\n\n(4) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible unless it is\nestablished that the suspect:\n\n(a) had been informed by a constable as described in\nsubsection 23WA(4); or\n\n(b) otherwise knew;\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 7\n\nSection 23YBA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthat the fact of refusing to comply with the direction, or\nobstructing, resisting, hindering, using violence against,\nthreatening or intimidating the person, in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure might be used in evidence\nagainst the suspect.\n\n(5) The court or jury may draw such inferences from the evidence\ndescribed in subsection (2) as appear to the court or jury to be\nproper in the circumstances, having regard to any evidence given\nby or on behalf of the suspect.\nSubdivision C—Application\n23YBA  Division does not apply to a proceeding in a foreign country\nor an international tribunal\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not apply in relation to a\nproceeding in a foreign country or international tribunal in which\nforensic evidence is provided in response to a request by:\n\n(a) a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an international tribunal; or\n\n(c) a foreign law enforcement agency.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies where a constable or magistrate has ordered\nthe carrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect under this\nPart.\n\n(2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), evidence that the suspect:\n\n(a) refused to comply with any reasonable direction in\nconnection with the carrying out of the forensic procedure; or\n\n(b) obstructed, resisted, hindered, used violence against,\nthreatened or intimidated a person in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure;\nis admissible in any proceedings against the suspect in respect of a\nrelevant offence.\n\n(3) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible if the\nforensic procedure was in fact carried out satisfactorily.\n\n(4) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible unless it is\nestablished that the suspect:\n\n(a) had been informed by a constable as described in\nsubsection 23WA(4); or\n\n(b) otherwise knew;\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 7\n\nSection 23YBA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthat the fact of refusing to comply with the direction, or\nobstructing, resisting, hindering, using violence against,\nthreatening or intimidating the person, in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure might be used in evidence\nagainst the suspect.\n\n(5) The court or jury may draw such inferences from the evidence\ndescribed in subsection (2) as appear to the court or jury to be\nproper in the circumstances, having regard to any evidence given\nby or on behalf of the suspect.\nSubdivision C—Application\n23YBA  Division does not apply to a proceeding in a foreign country\nor an international tribunal\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not apply in relation to a\nproceeding in a foreign country or international tribunal in which\nforensic evidence is provided in response to a request by:\n\n(a) a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an international tribunal; or\n\n(c) a foreign law enforcement agency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2d7458a2ac8eca53721323bfd1ad0112d6c46754a430d0a2fb37f169388a7734"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YB Obstructing the carrying out of forensic procedure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies where a constable or magistrate has ordered\nthe carrying out of a forensic procedure on a suspect under this\nPart.\n\n(2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), evidence that the suspect:\n\n(a) refused to comply with any reasonable direction in\nconnection with the carrying out of the forensic procedure; or\n\n(b) obstructed, resisted, hindered, used violence against,\nthreatened or intimidated a person in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure;\nis admissible in any proceedings against the suspect in respect of a\nrelevant offence.\n\n(3) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible if the\nforensic procedure was in fact carried out satisfactorily.\n\n(4) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible unless it is\nestablished that the suspect:\n\n(a) had been informed by a constable as described in\nsubsection 23WA(4); or\n\n(b) otherwise knew;\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 7\n\nSection 23YBA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthat the fact of refusing to comply with the direction, or\nobstructing, resisting, hindering, using violence against,\nthreatening or intimidating the person, in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure might be used in evidence\nagainst the suspect.\n\n(5) The court or jury may draw such inferences from the evidence\ndescribed in subsection (2) as appear to the court or jury to be\nproper in the circumstances, having regard to any evidence given\nby or on behalf of the suspect.\nSubdivision C—Application\n23YBA  Division does not apply to a proceeding in a foreign country\nor an international tribunal\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not apply in relation to a\nproceeding in a foreign country or international tribunal in which\nforensic evidence is provided in response to a request by:\n\n(a) a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an international tribunal; or\n\n(c) a foreign law enforcement agency."
    },
