    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YB(4) Obstructing the carrying out of forensic procedure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yb-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible unless it is\nestablished that the suspect:\n\n(a) had been informed by a constable as described in\nsubsection 23WA(4); or\n\n(b) otherwise knew;\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 7\n\nSection 23YBA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthat the fact of refusing to comply with the direction, or\nobstructing, resisting, hindering, using violence against,\nthreatening or intimidating the person, in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure might be used in evidence\nagainst the suspect.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible unless it is\nestablished that the suspect:\n\n(a) had been informed by a constable as described in\nsubsection 23WA(4); or\n\n(b) otherwise knew;\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 7\n\nSection 23YBA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthat the fact of refusing to comply with the direction, or\nobstructing, resisting, hindering, using violence against,\nthreatening or intimidating the person, in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure might be used in evidence\nagainst the suspect.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f7987aade7b2c8cedb737839fed70b547d611d1086f1b77b89fb3000172d9cb9",
      "skos:note": "Refusing to comply with direction or obstructing forensic procedure is not admissible as evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yb-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YB(4) Obstructing the carrying out of forensic procedure",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Evidence described in subsection (2) is not admissible unless it is\nestablished that the suspect:\n\n(a) had been informed by a constable as described in\nsubsection 23WA(4); or\n\n(b) otherwise knew;\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nAdmissibility of evidence  Division 7\n\nSection 23YBA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthat the fact of refusing to comply with the direction, or\nobstructing, resisting, hindering, using violence against,\nthreatening or intimidating the person, in connection with the\ncarrying out of the forensic procedure might be used in evidence\nagainst the suspect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
