      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of obstructing forensic procedure",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "State direction to suspect",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Refusal or obstruction is not admissible as evidence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YB(5) Obstructing the carrying out of forensic procedure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yb-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The court or jury may draw such inferences from the evidence\ndescribed in subsection (2) as appear to the court or jury to be\nproper in the circumstances, having regard to any evidence given\nby or on behalf of the suspect.\nSubdivision C—Application\n23YBA  Division does not apply to a proceeding in a foreign country\nor an international tribunal\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not apply in relation to a\nproceeding in a foreign country or international tribunal in which\nforensic evidence is provided in response to a request by:\n\n(a) a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an international tribunal; or\n\n(c) a foreign law enforcement agency.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The court or jury may draw such inferences from the evidence\ndescribed in subsection (2) as appear to the court or jury to be\nproper in the circumstances, having regard to any evidence given\nby or on behalf of the suspect.\nSubdivision C—Application\n23YBA  Division does not apply to a proceeding in a foreign country\nor an international tribunal\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not apply in relation to a\nproceeding in a foreign country or international tribunal in which\nforensic evidence is provided in response to a request by:\n\n(a) a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an international tribunal; or\n\n(c) a foreign law enforcement agency.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f9cfc71983c8fef37f82e32cdf0d3b4216f96da1b82409c357d54b9c9792bf8",
      "skos:note": "Does not apply to proceedings in foreign countries or international tribunals."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yb-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YB(5) Obstructing the carrying out of forensic procedure",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The court or jury may draw such inferences from the evidence\ndescribed in subsection (2) as appear to the court or jury to be\nproper in the circumstances, having regard to any evidence given\nby or on behalf of the suspect.\nSubdivision C—Application\n23YBA  Division does not apply to a proceeding in a foreign country\nor an international tribunal\n\nTo avoid doubt, this Division does not apply in relation to a\nproceeding in a foreign country or international tribunal in which\nforensic evidence is provided in response to a request by:\n\n(a) a foreign country; or\n\n(b) an international tribunal; or\n\n(c) a foreign law enforcement agency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yb-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Forbid",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Does not apply to proceedings in foreign countries or international tribunals.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YC Destruction of forensic material where interim order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "disallowed\n\n(1) If an interim order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure\nmade under section 23XA is disallowed after the forensic\nprocedure is carried out, the investigating constable must ensure\nthat:\n\n(a) all forensic material obtained as a result of the carrying out of\nthe procedure is destroyed as soon as practicable after the\ndisallowance; and\n\n(b) a copy of the results of any analysis of the forensic material\nare made available to the suspect.\nNote:\nDivision 9 contains provisions about making copies of material\navailable to the suspect.\n\n(2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under\nsection 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under\nsection 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material\nobtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be\nretained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the end of the period.",
      "skos:definition": "disallowed\n\n(1) If an interim order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure\nmade under section 23XA is disallowed after the forensic\nprocedure is carried out, the investigating constable must ensure\nthat:\n\n(a) all forensic material obtained as a result of the carrying out of\nthe procedure is destroyed as soon as practicable after the\ndisallowance; and\n\n(b) a copy of the results of any analysis of the forensic material\nare made available to the suspect.\nNote:\nDivision 9 contains provisions about making copies of material\navailable to the suspect.\n\n(2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under\nsection 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under\nsection 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material\nobtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be\nretained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the end of the period.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yc-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d6ab5f3fc6d8e40faec01b06b0c0ce791abab24362e5880ddfacb9f449a5dee"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YC Destruction of forensic material where interim order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "disallowed\n\n(1) If an interim order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure\nmade under section 23XA is disallowed after the forensic\nprocedure is carried out, the investigating constable must ensure\nthat:\n\n(a) all forensic material obtained as a result of the carrying out of\nthe procedure is destroyed as soon as practicable after the\ndisallowance; and\n\n(b) a copy of the results of any analysis of the forensic material\nare made available to the suspect.\nNote:\nDivision 9 contains provisions about making copies of material\navailable to the suspect.\n\n(2) If an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure made under\nsection 23XWU or for the retention of forensic material under\nsection 23XWV specifies a period for which forensic material\nobtained as a result of the carrying out of the procedure may be\nretained, the forensic material is to be destroyed as soon as\npracticable after the end of the period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yc-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YC(1) Destruction of forensic material where interim order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yc-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
