    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-6-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits reckless matching of DNA profiles.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the person’s conduct causes the matching that is not permitted by this Part of a DNA profile...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Imprisonment for 2 years."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-6-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits reckless conduct.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the person is reckless as to any such matching of profiles.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Imprisonment for 2 years."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-6-2-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Imply",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Implies imprisonment if reckless conduct occurs.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the person is reckless as to any such matching of profiles.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Imprisonment for 2 years."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-6-2-ss-2-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must ensure removal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "No identifying information should be retained",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Offence if not removed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ye",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YE Powers etc. of legal representatives and interview friends",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23ye"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A request or objection that may be made by a suspect or offender\nunder this Part may be made on the suspect’s or offender’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in any case—the suspect’s or offender’s legal representative;\nor\n\n(b) if the suspect or offender is a child or an incapable person—\nan interview friend of the suspect or offender; or\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect or offender is an Aboriginal person or a\nTorres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the suspect or\noffender.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a provision of this Part requires a suspect or offender to be\ninformed of a matter; and\n\n(b) an interview friend or legal representative of the suspect is\npresent when the suspect or offender is to be so informed;\nand\n\n(c) the suspect or offender is so informed in a language\n(including in sign language or braille) in which the suspect’s\nor offender’s interview friend or legal representative is not\nable to communicate with reasonable fluency;\nthe interview friend or legal representative must also be informed\nof the matter in a language in which the interview friend or legal\nrepresentative is able to communicate with reasonable fluency.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A request or objection that may be made by a suspect or offender\nunder this Part may be made on the suspect’s or offender’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in any case—the suspect’s or offender’s legal representative;\nor\n\n(b) if the suspect or offender is a child or an incapable person—\nan interview friend of the suspect or offender; or\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect or offender is an Aboriginal person or a\nTorres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the suspect or\noffender.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a provision of this Part requires a suspect or offender to be\ninformed of a matter; and\n\n(b) an interview friend or legal representative of the suspect is\npresent when the suspect or offender is to be so informed;\nand\n\n(c) the suspect or offender is so informed in a language\n(including in sign language or braille) in which the suspect’s\nor offender’s interview friend or legal representative is not\nable to communicate with reasonable fluency;\nthe interview friend or legal representative must also be informed\nof the matter in a language in which the interview friend or legal\nrepresentative is able to communicate with reasonable fluency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ye-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ye-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9c59c351f02163e91f8732624d2583b598ff61182d6c56777acca803882285e7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23ye",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YE Powers etc. of legal representatives and interview friends",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A request or objection that may be made by a suspect or offender\nunder this Part may be made on the suspect’s or offender’s behalf\nby:\n\n(a) in any case—the suspect’s or offender’s legal representative;\nor\n\n(b) if the suspect or offender is a child or an incapable person—\nan interview friend of the suspect or offender; or\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect or offender is an Aboriginal person or a\nTorres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the suspect or\noffender.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) a provision of this Part requires a suspect or offender to be\ninformed of a matter; and\n\n(b) an interview friend or legal representative of the suspect is\npresent when the suspect or offender is to be so informed;\nand\n\n(c) the suspect or offender is so informed in a language\n(including in sign language or braille) in which the suspect’s\nor offender’s interview friend or legal representative is not\nable to communicate with reasonable fluency;\nthe interview friend or legal representative must also be informed\nof the matter in a language in which the interview friend or legal\nrepresentative is able to communicate with reasonable fluency."
    },
