    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YF(2) Obligation of investigating constables relating to tape",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yf-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.116",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where an investigating constable is required to ensure that a\nsuspect, offender or volunteer is given an opportunity to view a\nvideo recording made under this Part, the investigating constable\nmust ensure that the same opportunity is given to:\n\n(a) in any case—the suspect’s, offender’s or volunteer’s legal\nrepresentative; and\n\n(b) if the suspect, offender or volunteer is a child or an incapable\nperson—an interview friend of the suspect, offender or\nvolunteer; and\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect, offender or volunteer is an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the\nsuspect, offender or volunteer.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Where an investigating constable is required to ensure that a\nsuspect, offender or volunteer is given an opportunity to view a\nvideo recording made under this Part, the investigating constable\nmust ensure that the same opportunity is given to:\n\n(a) in any case—the suspect’s, offender’s or volunteer’s legal\nrepresentative; and\n\n(b) if the suspect, offender or volunteer is a child or an incapable\nperson—an interview friend of the suspect, offender or\nvolunteer; and\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect, offender or volunteer is an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the\nsuspect, offender or volunteer.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yf-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yf-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b446c4de4f13641effe13ff19598b61f7b1b9889b8ec4dd5be3b81a69877028",
      "skos:note": "Investigating constable must provide suspect, offender or volunteer with opportunity to view video recording.",
      "dc:description": "opportunity to view video recording"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YF(2) Obligation of investigating constables relating to tape",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 116,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where an investigating constable is required to ensure that a\nsuspect, offender or volunteer is given an opportunity to view a\nvideo recording made under this Part, the investigating constable\nmust ensure that the same opportunity is given to:\n\n(a) in any case—the suspect’s, offender’s or volunteer’s legal\nrepresentative; and\n\n(b) if the suspect, offender or volunteer is a child or an incapable\nperson—an interview friend of the suspect, offender or\nvolunteer; and\n\n(c) if the investigating constable believes on reasonable grounds\nthat the suspect, offender or volunteer is an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—an interview friend of the\nsuspect, offender or volunteer."
    },
