    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YG Material required to be made available to suspect, offender or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "volunteer\n\n(1) Material from samples, copies, or any other material, that must be\nmade available to a suspect, offender or volunteer under this Part:\n\n(a) may be sent to the suspect, offender or volunteer at his or her\nlast known address (if any), or to the suspect’s, offender’s or\nvolunteer’s legal representative (if any) at his or her last\nknown address; or\n\n(b) if there is no known address as mentioned in paragraph (a)—\nmay be made available for collection by the suspect, offender\nor volunteer at the police station where the investigating\nconstable was based at the time the forensic procedure was\ncarried out.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), material of any kind that is required by\nthis Part to be made available to a suspect, offender or volunteer\nmust be made available in accordance with subsection (1):\n\n(a) within 14 days after the material comes into existence; or\n\n(b) if the material is requested by the suspect, offender or\nvolunteer or the suspect’s, offender’s or volunteer’s interview\nfriend or legal representative, within 14 days of the request.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to:\n\n(a) copies of records required to be made available under\nsubsection 23XE(5); and\n\n(b) material required to be provided under section 23XU; and\n\n(c) copies of results of analysis and other information required to\nbe provided under section 23XW.",
      "skos:definition": "volunteer\n\n(1) Material from samples, copies, or any other material, that must be\nmade available to a suspect, offender or volunteer under this Part:\n\n(a) may be sent to the suspect, offender or volunteer at his or her\nlast known address (if any), or to the suspect’s, offender’s or\nvolunteer’s legal representative (if any) at his or her last\nknown address; or\n\n(b) if there is no known address as mentioned in paragraph (a)—\nmay be made available for collection by the suspect, offender\nor volunteer at the police station where the investigating\nconstable was based at the time the forensic procedure was\ncarried out.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), material of any kind that is required by\nthis Part to be made available to a suspect, offender or volunteer\nmust be made available in accordance with subsection (1):\n\n(a) within 14 days after the material comes into existence; or\n\n(b) if the material is requested by the suspect, offender or\nvolunteer or the suspect’s, offender’s or volunteer’s interview\nfriend or legal representative, within 14 days of the request.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to:\n\n(a) copies of records required to be made available under\nsubsection 23XE(5); and\n\n(b) material required to be provided under section 23XU; and\n\n(c) copies of results of analysis and other information required to\nbe provided under section 23XW.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yg-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dcbb0f3cafb30402d5ed4cb826e000bcae930c7ce60763e0458665150dffa879"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YG Material required to be made available to suspect, offender or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "volunteer\n\n(1) Material from samples, copies, or any other material, that must be\nmade available to a suspect, offender or volunteer under this Part:\n\n(a) may be sent to the suspect, offender or volunteer at his or her\nlast known address (if any), or to the suspect’s, offender’s or\nvolunteer’s legal representative (if any) at his or her last\nknown address; or\n\n(b) if there is no known address as mentioned in paragraph (a)—\nmay be made available for collection by the suspect, offender\nor volunteer at the police station where the investigating\nconstable was based at the time the forensic procedure was\ncarried out.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), material of any kind that is required by\nthis Part to be made available to a suspect, offender or volunteer\nmust be made available in accordance with subsection (1):\n\n(a) within 14 days after the material comes into existence; or\n\n(b) if the material is requested by the suspect, offender or\nvolunteer or the suspect’s, offender’s or volunteer’s interview\nfriend or legal representative, within 14 days of the request.\n\n(3) Subsection (2) does not apply to:\n\n(a) copies of records required to be made available under\nsubsection 23XE(5); and\n\n(b) material required to be provided under section 23XU; and\n\n(c) copies of results of analysis and other information required to\nbe provided under section 23XW."
    },
