      "values:originalText": "(3) Forensic material, or information obtained from it, that is taken in\naccordance with a law of a State or a Territory, as in force\nimmediately before the commencement of this subsection, may be\nretained or used for investigative, evidentiary or statistical\npurposes of the Commonwealth. The material or information may\nbe retained or used even if its retention or use would, but for this\nsubsection, constitute a breach of, or failure to comply with, any\nprovision of this Part relating to the carrying out of forensic\nprocedures."
    },
