    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YQ Commissioner may delegate functions and powers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.124",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police may delegate\nall or any of his or her functions and powers under this Part to a\nconstable or AFP appointee.\n\n(2) In subsection (1), AFP appointee has the meaning it has in the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nCarrying out forensic procedures at the request of a foreign country or international\ntribunal  Division 9A\n\nSection 23YQA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner of the Australian Federal Police may delegate\nall or any of his or her functions and powers under this Part to a\nconstable or AFP appointee.\n\n(2) In subsection (1), AFP appointee has the meaning it has in the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nCarrying out forensic procedures at the request of a foreign country or international\ntribunal  Division 9A\n\nSection 23YQA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
