      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Nothing in this Part is intended to limit the rights and protections\nprovided by Part IC to the extent that the provisions of that\nPart can operate in circumstances covered by this Part.\n\n(2) The rights and protections conferred by this Part are in addition to\nthose conferred by Part IC but, to the extent (if any) that\ncompliance with this Part results in compliance with Part IC, the\nrequirements of Part IC are satisfied.\n\n\nForensic procedures  Part ID\nOperation of this Part and effect on other laws  Division 10\n\nSection 23YU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
