    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23YU Application of other laws",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Part is not intended to limit or exclude the operation of\nanother law of the Commonwealth or of a law of a State or\nTerritory relating to:\n\n(a) the carrying out of forensic procedures, including procedures\nnot referred to in this Part; or\n\n(aa) without limiting paragraph (a), the carrying out of breath\nanalysis or a breath test or the production of samples of blood\nand urine to determine the level of alcohol or drugs, if any,\npresent in a person’s body; or\n\n(b) the taking of forensic samples, including samples not referred\nto in this Part; or\n\n(c) the taking of identification evidence; or\n\n(d) the carrying out of searches of the person; or\n\n(e) the retention or use of forensic material or information\nobtained as a result of activities described in paragraphs (a),\n(b), (c) and (d).\n\n(2) To avoid any doubt, it is declared that even though another law of\nthe Commonwealth provides power to do one or more of the things\nreferred to in subsection (1), a similar power conferred by this Part\nmay be used despite the existence of the power under the other\nlaw.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This Part is not intended to limit or exclude the operation of\nanother law of the Commonwealth or of a law of a State or\nTerritory relating to:\n\n(a) the carrying out of forensic procedures, including procedures\nnot referred to in this Part; or\n\n(aa) without limiting paragraph (a), the carrying out of breath\nanalysis or a breath test or the production of samples of blood\nand urine to determine the level of alcohol or drugs, if any,\npresent in a person’s body; or\n\n(b) the taking of forensic samples, including samples not referred\nto in this Part; or\n\n(c) the taking of identification evidence; or\n\n(d) the carrying out of searches of the person; or\n\n(e) the retention or use of forensic material or information\nobtained as a result of activities described in paragraphs (a),\n(b), (c) and (d).\n\n(2) To avoid any doubt, it is declared that even though another law of\nthe Commonwealth provides power to do one or more of the things\nreferred to in subsection (1), a similar power conferred by this Part\nmay be used despite the existence of the power under the other\nlaw.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yu-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23yu-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bc780b1df499cd94599dd1f0ffa140053e15d6e9f051c31307875816944e9de5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23yu",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23YU Application of other laws",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Part is not intended to limit or exclude the operation of\nanother law of the Commonwealth or of a law of a State or\nTerritory relating to:\n\n(a) the carrying out of forensic procedures, including procedures\nnot referred to in this Part; or\n\n(aa) without limiting paragraph (a), the carrying out of breath\nanalysis or a breath test or the production of samples of blood\nand urine to determine the level of alcohol or drugs, if any,\npresent in a person’s body; or\n\n(b) the taking of forensic samples, including samples not referred\nto in this Part; or\n\n(c) the taking of identification evidence; or\n\n(d) the carrying out of searches of the person; or\n\n(e) the retention or use of forensic material or information\nobtained as a result of activities described in paragraphs (a),\n(b), (c) and (d).\n\n(2) To avoid any doubt, it is declared that even though another law of\nthe Commonwealth provides power to do one or more of the things\nreferred to in subsection (1), a similar power conferred by this Part\nmay be used despite the existence of the power under the other\nlaw."
    },
