    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zb-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23ZB(6) Forfeiture of material by operation of law",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23zb-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.140",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If there is an objection described in paragraph (3)(c) but the head\nof the police force that includes the constable considers that the\nforfeitable thing should be forfeited to the Commonwealth despite\nthe objection:\n\n(a) the head of the police force must instruct the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions to apply for an order under section 23ZD\nfor the forfeiture of the thing; and\n\n(b) the Director must make the application.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If there is an objection described in paragraph (3)(c) but the head\nof the police force that includes the constable considers that the\nforfeitable thing should be forfeited to the Commonwealth despite\nthe objection:\n\n(a) the head of the police force must instruct the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions to apply for an order under section 23ZD\nfor the forfeiture of the thing; and\n\n(b) the Director must make the application.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zb-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zb-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zb-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zb-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b80e4784025aa51dc4b177810cc6b2c8009cb5dc9cf15a06dbc9a39b3f9bdc0c",
      "skos:note": "Head of police force must instruct Director to apply for forfeiture order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23zb-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23ZB(6) Forfeiture of material by operation of law",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 140,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If there is an objection described in paragraph (3)(c) but the head\nof the police force that includes the constable considers that the\nforfeitable thing should be forfeited to the Commonwealth despite\nthe objection:\n\n(a) the head of the police force must instruct the Director of\nPublic Prosecutions to apply for an order under section 23ZD\nfor the forfeiture of the thing; and\n\n(b) the Director must make the application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zb-ss-6-norm",
