    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23ZD(5) Forfeiture of material by court order on application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23zd-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.144",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The court may order the Commonwealth to pay a specified\nreasonable amount of compensation to a person who owns, has a\nright to possess or has other property in a thing whose forfeiture\nthe court orders if the thing is a computer, data storage device or\nother electronic equipment and the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has appeared at the hearing of the application; and\n\n(b) the person did not commit, is not and has not been convicted\n(by the court or another court) of, and has not been found by\nanother court in civil proceedings to have committed, the\nCommonwealth child sex offence; and\n\n(c) the person is not the subject of proceedings in another court\nrelating to the Commonwealth child sex offence and has not\nbeen the subject of such proceedings in connection with\nwhich an appeal may still be lodged as of right; and\n\n(d) the person is not the subject of an investigation into a\nCommonwealth child sex offence of which the thing provides\nevidence.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The court may order the Commonwealth to pay a specified\nreasonable amount of compensation to a person who owns, has a\nright to possess or has other property in a thing whose forfeiture\nthe court orders if the thing is a computer, data storage device or\nother electronic equipment and the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has appeared at the hearing of the application; and\n\n(b) the person did not commit, is not and has not been convicted\n(by the court or another court) of, and has not been found by\nanother court in civil proceedings to have committed, the\nCommonwealth child sex offence; and\n\n(c) the person is not the subject of proceedings in another court\nrelating to the Commonwealth child sex offence and has not\nbeen the subject of such proceedings in connection with\nwhich an appeal may still be lodged as of right; and\n\n(d) the person is not the subject of an investigation into a\nCommonwealth child sex offence of which the thing provides\nevidence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b1d427d7f09ea1aedc5eba0e9295b5e273c6b9953f6157336600b2736961021",
      "skos:note": "The court may order the Commonwealth to pay compensation to a person who owns or has property in electronic equipment under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23zd-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23ZD(5) Forfeiture of material by court order on application",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 144,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The court may order the Commonwealth to pay a specified\nreasonable amount of compensation to a person who owns, has a\nright to possess or has other property in a thing whose forfeiture\nthe court orders if the thing is a computer, data storage device or\nother electronic equipment and the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the person has appeared at the hearing of the application; and\n\n(b) the person did not commit, is not and has not been convicted\n(by the court or another court) of, and has not been found by\nanother court in civil proceedings to have committed, the\nCommonwealth child sex offence; and\n\n(c) the person is not the subject of proceedings in another court\nrelating to the Commonwealth child sex offence and has not\nbeen the subject of such proceedings in connection with\nwhich an appeal may still be lodged as of right; and\n\n(d) the person is not the subject of an investigation into a\nCommonwealth child sex offence of which the thing provides\nevidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5-norm",
