      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "before",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The person did not commit, is not and has not been convicted of, the Commonwealth child sex offence before the hearing.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Person A did not commit, is not and has not been convicted of, the Commonwealth child sex offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Person A is not guilty of the crime."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23zd-ss-5-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "and",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The person is not the subject of proceedings in another court relating to the Commonwealth child sex offence and has not been the subject of such proceedings in connection with which an appeal may still be lodged as of right.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Person A is not the subject of proceedings in another court relating to the Commonwealth child sex offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Person A is not under investigation for the crime."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ze",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23ZE Effect of forfeiture under this Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23ze"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.147",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a thing is forfeited to the Commonwealth\nunder this Part.\n\n(2) When the thing is forfeited it becomes the property of the\nCommonwealth.\n\n(3) A constable may, without warrant, seize the thing.\n\n(4) The Commissioner may deal with the thing in any way he or she\nconsiders appropriate (including by destroying the thing).\n\n(5) However, if the thing is in the custody of a constable who is a\nmember of a police force of a State or Territory, the head of the\npolice force may deal with the thing in any way he or she considers\nappropriate (including by destroying the thing).\n\n(6) Subsections (3), (4) and (5) have effect despite section 9.\n23ZF  Compensation for forfeiture of electronic equipment etc.\n\n(1) This section applies to a person if:\n\n(a) a thing that is a computer, data storage device or other\nelectronic equipment is forfeited under this Part; and\n\n(b) the person owned, had a right to possess or had other\nproperty in the thing immediately before the forfeiture.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth is liable to pay the person a reasonable\namount of compensation for the forfeiture.\n\n(3) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in a\ncourt of competent jurisdiction of a State or Territory for the",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if a thing is forfeited to the Commonwealth\nunder this Part.\n\n(2) When the thing is forfeited it becomes the property of the\nCommonwealth.\n\n(3) A constable may, without warrant, seize the thing.\n\n(4) The Commissioner may deal with the thing in any way he or she\nconsiders appropriate (including by destroying the thing).\n\n(5) However, if the thing is in the custody of a constable who is a\nmember of a police force of a State or Territory, the head of the\npolice force may deal with the thing in any way he or she considers\nappropriate (including by destroying the thing).\n\n(6) Subsections (3), (4) and (5) have effect despite section 9.\n23ZF  Compensation for forfeiture of electronic equipment etc.\n\n(1) This section applies to a person if:\n\n(a) a thing that is a computer, data storage device or other\nelectronic equipment is forfeited under this Part; and\n\n(b) the person owned, had a right to possess or had other\nproperty in the thing immediately before the forfeiture.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth is liable to pay the person a reasonable\namount of compensation for the forfeiture.\n\n(3) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in a\ncourt of competent jurisdiction of a State or Territory for the",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ze-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23ze-ss-2"
