    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41(2) Conspiracy to bring false accusation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-41-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For a person to be guilty of an offence against subsection (1):\n\n(a) the person must have entered into an agreement with one or\nmore other persons; and\n\n(b) the person and at least one other party to the agreement must\nhave intended that a person be charged falsely with an\noffence pursuant to the agreement; and\n\n(c) the person or at least one other party to the agreement must\nhave committed an overt act pursuant to the agreement.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For a person to be guilty of an offence against subsection (1):\n\n(a) the person must have entered into an agreement with one or\nmore other persons; and\n\n(b) the person and at least one other party to the agreement must\nhave intended that a person be charged falsely with an\noffence pursuant to the agreement; and\n\n(c) the person or at least one other party to the agreement must\nhave committed an overt act pursuant to the agreement.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-2-norm"
