      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) For a person to be guilty of an offence against subsection (1):",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the person or at least one other party to the agreement must have committed an overt act pursuant to the agreement;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "during",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Overt act must occur during agreement period",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) For a person to be guilty of an offence against subsection (1):",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the overt act must have occurred during the time the agreement was in effect;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-2-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires at least one other party for conspiracy",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) For a person to be guilty of an offence against subsection (1):",
      "cml:conclusionText": "at least one other party to the agreement must have intended that a person be charged falsely with an offence pursuant to the agreement;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41(3) Conspiracy to bring false accusation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-41-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if:\n\n(a) charging a person falsely pursuant to the agreement is\nimpossible; or\n\n(b) the only other party to the agreement is a body corporate; or\n\n(c) each other party to the agreement is a person who is not\ncriminally responsible; or\n\n\nOffences relating to the administration of justice  Part III\nPerverting the course of justice  Division 4\n\nSection 42\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) subject to subsection (4), all other parties to the agreement\nhave been acquitted of the offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if:\n\n(a) charging a person falsely pursuant to the agreement is\nimpossible; or\n\n(b) the only other party to the agreement is a body corporate; or\n\n(c) each other party to the agreement is a person who is not\ncriminally responsible; or\n\n\nOffences relating to the administration of justice  Part III\nPerverting the course of justice  Division 4\n\nSection 42\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) subject to subsection (4), all other parties to the agreement\nhave been acquitted of the offence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a18ddc2fc95888a489f2f05c48faf71e9a2da3f6e731e10e3d46b21974420550",
      "skos:note": "A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-41-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41(3) Conspiracy to bring false accusation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A person may be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1)\neven if:\n\n(a) charging a person falsely pursuant to the agreement is\nimpossible; or\n\n(b) the only other party to the agreement is a body corporate; or\n\n(c) each other party to the agreement is a person who is not\ncriminally responsible; or\n\n\nOffences relating to the administration of justice  Part III\nPerverting the course of justice  Division 4\n\nSection 42\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) subject to subsection (4), all other parties to the agreement\nhave been acquitted of the offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
