    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41(4) Conspiracy to bring false accusation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-41-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) all other parties to the agreement have been acquitted of such\nan offence; and\n\n(b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) all other parties to the agreement have been acquitted of such\nan offence; and\n\n(b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ddb15bd569ef1fe8a4a4a1ff1b06d3c5d2e358e023cefae65971ebf49b296e50",
      "skos:note": "No person can be found guilty of an offence against subsection (1) if all other parties to the agreement have been acquitted of such an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-41-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41(4) Conspiracy to bring false accusation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person cannot be found guilty of an offence against\nsubsection (1) if:\n\n(a) all other parties to the agreement have been acquitted of such\nan offence; and\n\n(b) a finding of guilt would be inconsistent with their acquittal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-41-ss-4-norm",
