    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48 Harbouring etc. an escapee",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.168",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n\nOffences relating to the administration of justice  Part III\nEscape from criminal detention  Division 5\n\nSection 48A\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the first person knows that another person (the escapee) has\nescaped from a place where the other person was held in\ncriminal detention; and\n\n(b) the first person harbours, maintains or employs the escapee;\nand\n\n(c) the detention was lawful federal criminal detention.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n\nOffences relating to the administration of justice  Part III\nEscape from criminal detention  Division 5\n\nSection 48A\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the first person knows that another person (the escapee) has\nescaped from a place where the other person was held in\ncriminal detention; and\n\n(b) the first person harbours, maintains or employs the escapee;\nand\n\n(c) the detention was lawful federal criminal detention.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-48-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-48-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a9c9d29fa1833a3a82e4beb98359f034d7447bf0c075b896da492b42e9b55ecc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48 Harbouring etc. an escapee",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 168,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n\nOffences relating to the administration of justice  Part III\nEscape from criminal detention  Division 5\n\nSection 48A\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the first person knows that another person (the escapee) has\nescaped from a place where the other person was held in\ncriminal detention; and\n\n(b) the first person harbours, maintains or employs the escapee;\nand\n\n(c) the detention was lawful federal criminal detention.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(c) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code."
    },
