    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-49",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49 Removing property under seizure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-49"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or\nauthority of a court; and\n\n(b) the court was:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; and\n\n(c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of\nthe property; and\n\n(d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or\ndefeating the attachment or process.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\n\n\nPiracy  Part IV\n\nSection 51\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or\nauthority of a court; and\n\n(b) the court was:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; and\n\n(c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of\nthe property; and\n\n(d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or\ndefeating the attachment or process.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\n\n\nPiracy  Part IV\n\nSection 51\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-49-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-49-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f92ec454e579232c9151e431d37298f29ecf8442ab22b0333e1e24aaf0976ec5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-49",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49 Removing property under seizure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) property has been attached, or taken, under the process or\nauthority of a court; and\n\n(b) the court was:\n\n(i) a federal court; or\n\n(ii) exercising federal jurisdiction; or\n\n(iii) a court of a Territory; and\n\n(c) the person receives, removes, retains, conceals or disposes of\nthe property; and\n\n(d) the person does so with the intention of hindering or\ndefeating the attachment or process.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraph (1)(b) element of the\noffence.\nNote:\nFor absolute liability, see section 6.2 of the Criminal Code.\n\n\nPiracy  Part IV\n\nSection 51\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
