    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-55",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55 Written consent of Attorney-General required",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-55"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A prosecution for an offence against this Part requires the consent\nof the Attorney-General.\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1):\n\n(a) a person may be arrested for an offence referred to in\nsubsection (1), and a warrant for such an arrest may be issued\nand executed; and\n\n(b) a person may be charged with such an offence; and\n\n(c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail;\nbut no further step in the proceedings referred to in subsection (1)\nis to be taken until the Attorney-General’s consent has been given.\n\n(3) Nothing in subsection (2) prevents the discharge of the accused if\nproceedings are not continued within a reasonable time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A prosecution for an offence against this Part requires the consent\nof the Attorney-General.\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1):\n\n(a) a person may be arrested for an offence referred to in\nsubsection (1), and a warrant for such an arrest may be issued\nand executed; and\n\n(b) a person may be charged with such an offence; and\n\n(c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail;\nbut no further step in the proceedings referred to in subsection (1)\nis to be taken until the Attorney-General’s consent has been given.\n\n(3) Nothing in subsection (2) prevents the discharge of the accused if\nproceedings are not continued within a reasonable time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-55-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-55-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-55-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2ff7762e6c4d8ec73ac28021e31c053e064b639da6c16f12c358c73890aef65c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-55",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55 Written consent of Attorney-General required",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A prosecution for an offence against this Part requires the consent\nof the Attorney-General.\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1):\n\n(a) a person may be arrested for an offence referred to in\nsubsection (1), and a warrant for such an arrest may be issued\nand executed; and\n\n(b) a person may be charged with such an offence; and\n\n(c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail;\nbut no further step in the proceedings referred to in subsection (1)\nis to be taken until the Attorney-General’s consent has been given.\n\n(3) Nothing in subsection (2) prevents the discharge of the accused if\nproceedings are not continued within a reasonable time."
    },
