      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A certificate by the Foreign Affairs Minister, or by an eligible\nperson authorised by that Minister to make such a certificate,\nstating that:\n\n(a) specified waters were, at a specified time:\n\n(i) part of the high seas; or\n\n(ii) within the coastal sea of Australia; or\n\n(b) a specified place was, at a specified time, a place beyond the\njurisdiction of any country;\nis, for the purposes of any proceedings for an offence against this\nPart, evidence of the facts stated in the certificate.\n\n(2) In this section:\neligible person means an SES employee in the Foreign Affairs\nDepartment.\n\n\nOffences relating to postal services  Part VIIA\n\nSection 85E\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A certificate by the Foreign Affairs Minister, or by an eligible\nperson authorised by that Minister to make such a certificate,\nstating that:\n\n(a) specified waters were, at a specified time:\n\n(i) part of the high seas; or\n\n(ii) within the coastal sea of Australia; or\n\n(b) a specified place was, at a specified time, a place beyond the\njurisdiction of any country;\nis, for the purposes of any proceedings for an offence against this\nPart, evidence of the facts stated in the certificate.\n\n(2) In this section:\neligible person means an SES employee in the Foreign Affairs\nDepartment.\n\n\nOffences relating to postal services  Part VIIA\n\nSection 85E\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
