      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.176",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person shall not make, use, have in his or her possession, or sell\nor otherwise dispose of, any article resembling, apparently\nintended to resemble or pass for, or likely to be mistaken for, an\nenvelope, letter-card, aerogram or other article on which Australia\nPost has caused a postage stamp to be affixed or printed, knowing\nthat it is not such an article.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person shall not make, use, have in his or her possession, or sell\nor otherwise dispose of, any article resembling, apparently\nintended to resemble or pass for, or likely to be mistaken for, an\nenvelope, letter-card, aerogram or other article on which Australia\nPost has caused a postage stamp to be affixed or printed, knowing\nthat it is not such an article.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years.",
