    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85z",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "85Z Articles carried by post to be taken to be Australia Post’s",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85z"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.183",
      "values:originalText": "property\n\nFor the purpose of any prosecution for an offence in relation to an\narticle carried by post or under the control of Australia Post, the\narticle shall be taken to be the property of Australia Post.\n85ZA  Postage stamps to be valuable securities etc.\n\nA postage stamp, and any document issued by Australia Post in\nrelation to the carriage by post of money or a direction to pay an\namount of money, shall be taken to be a valuable security for the\npurposes of any law relating to larceny.",
      "skos:definition": "property\n\nFor the purpose of any prosecution for an offence in relation to an\narticle carried by post or under the control of Australia Post, the\narticle shall be taken to be the property of Australia Post.\n85ZA  Postage stamps to be valuable securities etc.\n\nA postage stamp, and any document issued by Australia Post in\nrelation to the carriage by post of money or a direction to pay an\namount of money, shall be taken to be a valuable security for the\npurposes of any law relating to larceny.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85z-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85z-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6a3437f3c3e98a507661f23331e41f09b372917c1385d09d4be169008c5f1ff8",
      "skos:note": "Article carried by post is taken to be Australia Post's property for prosecution purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85z",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "85Z Articles carried by post to be taken to be Australia Post’s",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 183,
      "values:originalText": "property\n\nFor the purpose of any prosecution for an offence in relation to an\narticle carried by post or under the control of Australia Post, the\narticle shall be taken to be the property of Australia Post.\n85ZA  Postage stamps to be valuable securities etc.\n\nA postage stamp, and any document issued by Australia Post in\nrelation to the carriage by post of money or a direction to pay an\namount of money, shall be taken to be a valuable security for the\npurposes of any law relating to larceny."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85z-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85z"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85z-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "takes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Article is taken to be Australia Post's property",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "85ZL Interpretation of Part",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\nAUSTRAC means the Australian Transaction Reports and Analysis\nCentre continued in existence by the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006.\nCommonwealth authority means:\n\n(a) a Commonwealth Minister;\n\n(b) a Commonwealth Department;\n\n(ba) the Defence Force;\n\n(c) a body (whether incorporated or not), or a tribunal,\nestablished or appointed for a public purpose by or under a\nCommonwealth law, not being:\n\n(i) an incorporated company, society or association; or\n\n(ii) an organisation registered, or an association recognised,\nunder the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act\n2009, or a branch of such an organisation or association;\n\n(d) a body established or appointed by the Governor-General, or\nby a Commonwealth Minister, otherwise than by or under a\nCommonwealth law;\n\n(e) a person holding or performing the duties of an office\nestablished by or under, or an appointment made under, a\nCommonwealth law other than the office of Secretary of a\nCommonwealth Department;\n\n(f) a person holding or performing the duties of an appointment\nmade by the Governor-General, or by a Commonwealth\nMinister, otherwise than under a Commonwealth law;\n\n(g) a federal court;\n\n\nPardons, quashed convictions and spent convictions  Part VIIC\nInterpretation and application of Part  Division 1\n\nSection 85ZL\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(h) the Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory; or\n\n(j) the Australian Federal Police.\nCommonwealth Department means an Agency within the meaning\nof the Public Service Act 1999.\nCommonwealth law means:\n\n(a) an Act other than:\n\n(i) the Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act\n1988; or\n\n(ii) the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978;\n\n(b) an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws) made\nunder an Act (other than an Act referred to in\nsubparagraph (a)(i) or (ii)); or\n\n(c) any other legislation that applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth (other than legislation in so far as it is\napplied by an Act referred to in subparagraph (a)(i) or (ii)), to\nthe extent that it operates as such a law.\nCommonwealth Minister means a Minister of State of the\nCommonwealth.\nCommonwealth offence means an offence against a\nCommonwealth law.\ncomplaint means a complaint under subsection 85ZZA(1).\ndesignated offence means:\n\n(a) a sexual offence; or\n\n(b) any other offence against the person if the victim of the\noffence was under 18 at the time the offence was committed.\ndesignated position means a position in a Commonwealth\nauthority which the head of the authority has determined to be a\ndesignated security assessment position whose duties are likely to\ninvolve access to national security information classified as secret\nor top secret.\nforeign law means a law of a foreign country.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\nAUSTRAC means the Australian Transaction Reports and Analysis\nCentre continued in existence by the Anti-Money Laundering and\nCounter-Terrorism Financing Act 2006.\nCommonwealth authority means:\n\n(a) a Commonwealth Minister;\n\n(b) a Commonwealth Department;\n\n(ba) the Defence Force;\n\n(c) a body (whether incorporated or not), or a tribunal,\nestablished or appointed for a public purpose by or under a\nCommonwealth law, not being:\n\n(i) an incorporated company, society or association; or\n\n(ii) an organisation registered, or an association recognised,\nunder the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act\n2009, or a branch of such an organisation or association;\n\n(d) a body established or appointed by the Governor-General, or\nby a Commonwealth Minister, otherwise than by or under a\nCommonwealth law;\n\n(e) a person holding or performing the duties of an office\nestablished by or under, or an appointment made under, a\nCommonwealth law other than the office of Secretary of a\nCommonwealth Department;\n\n(f) a person holding or performing the duties of an appointment\nmade by the Governor-General, or by a Commonwealth\nMinister, otherwise than under a Commonwealth law;\n\n(g) a federal court;\n\n\nPardons, quashed convictions and spent convictions  Part VIIC\nInterpretation and application of Part  Division 1\n\nSection 85ZL\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(h) the Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory; or\n\n(j) the Australian Federal Police.\nCommonwealth Department means an Agency within the meaning\nof the Public Service Act 1999.\nCommonwealth law means:\n\n(a) an Act other than:\n\n(i) the Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act\n1988; or\n\n(ii) the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978;\n\n(b) an instrument (including rules, regulations or by-laws) made\nunder an Act (other than an Act referred to in\nsubparagraph (a)(i) or (ii)); or\n\n(c) any other legislation that applies as a law of the\nCommonwealth (other ",
      "cml:asserts": [
