    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "85ZM Meaning of conviction and spent conviction",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.189",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a person shall be taken to have been\nconvicted of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been convicted, whether summarily or on\nindictment, of the offence;\n\n(b) the person has been charged with, and found guilty of, the\noffence but discharged without conviction; or\n\n(c) the person has not been found guilty of the offence, but a\ncourt has taken it into account in passing sentence on the\nperson for another offence.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, a person’s conviction of an offence is\nspent if:\n\n(a) the person has been granted a pardon for a reason other than\nthat the person was wrongly convicted of the offence; or\n\n(b) the person was not sentenced to imprisonment for the\noffence, or was not sentenced to imprisonment for the\noffence for more than 30 months, and the waiting period for\nthe offence has ended.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a person shall be taken to have been\nconvicted of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been convicted, whether summarily or on\nindictment, of the offence;\n\n(b) the person has been charged with, and found guilty of, the\noffence but discharged without conviction; or\n\n(c) the person has not been found guilty of the offence, but a\ncourt has taken it into account in passing sentence on the\nperson for another offence.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, a person’s conviction of an offence is\nspent if:\n\n(a) the person has been granted a pardon for a reason other than\nthat the person was wrongly convicted of the offence; or\n\n(b) the person was not sentenced to imprisonment for the\noffence, or was not sentenced to imprisonment for the\noffence for more than 30 months, and the waiting period for\nthe offence has ended.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zm-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zm-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "553e2f852069412a7ca656bed8ca5638d8de8afeba02d3d4f3ec05e43846c233"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "85ZM Meaning of conviction and spent conviction",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 189,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a person shall be taken to have been\nconvicted of an offence if:\n\n(a) the person has been convicted, whether summarily or on\nindictment, of the offence;\n\n(b) the person has been charged with, and found guilty of, the\noffence but discharged without conviction; or\n\n(c) the person has not been found guilty of the offence, but a\ncourt has taken it into account in passing sentence on the\nperson for another offence.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, a person’s conviction of an offence is\nspent if:\n\n(a) the person has been granted a pardon for a reason other than\nthat the person was wrongly convicted of the offence; or\n\n(b) the person was not sentenced to imprisonment for the\noffence, or was not sentenced to imprisonment for the\noffence for more than 30 months, and the waiting period for\nthe offence has ended."
    },
