          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zr-ss-1-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c906a22f58b520f675dd2a7756be8b90fbf486c9e95cf9c0ce95aed690959006",
      "skos:note": "A person wrongly convicted of a Commonwealth offence is taken for all purposes as never having been convicted."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zr-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "85ZR(1) Pardons for persons wrongly convicted",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 191,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite any other Commonwealth law or any State law or Territory\nlaw, where a person has been granted a free and absolute pardon\nfor a Commonwealth offence or a Territory offence because the\nperson was wrongly convicted of the offence:\n\n(a) the person shall be taken, in any State or Territory, for all\npurposes, never to have been convicted of the offence; and\n\n(b) the person shall be taken, in a foreign country, by any\nCommonwealth authority or State authority in that country,\nfor all purposes, never to have been convicted of the offence."
    },
    {
