    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "85ZT Quashed convictions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.192",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to Division 6, but despite any other Commonwealth law or\nany State law or Territory law, where a person’s conviction of a\nCommonwealth offence or a Territory offence has been quashed,\nthe person is not required:\n\n(a) in any State or Territory—to disclose to any person, for any\npurpose, the fact that the person has been charged with, or\nconvicted of, the offence; or\n\n(b) in a foreign country—to disclose to any Commonwealth\nauthority or State authority in that country, for any purpose,\n\n\nPardons, quashed convictions and spent convictions  Part VIIC\nPardons for persons wrongly convicted, and quashed convictions  Division 2\n\nSection 85ZU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe fact that the person has been charged with, or convicted\nof, the offence.\n\n(2) Subject to Division 6, but despite any other Commonwealth law or\nany Territory law, where a person’s conviction of a State offence\nor a foreign offence has been quashed, the person is not required:\n\n(a) in any Territory—to disclose to any person, for any purpose,\nthe fact that the person has been charged with, or convicted\nof, the offence; or\n\n(b) in any State or foreign country—to disclose to any\nCommonwealth authority in that State or country, for any\npurpose, the fact that the person has been charged with, or\nconvicted of, the offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to Division 6, but despite any other Commonwealth law or\nany State law or Territory law, where a person’s conviction of a\nCommonwealth offence or a Territory offence has been quashed,\nthe person is not required:\n\n(a) in any State or Territory—to disclose to any person, for any\npurpose, the fact that the person has been charged with, or\nconvicted of, the offence; or\n\n(b) in a foreign country—to disclose to any Commonwealth\nauthority or State authority in that country, for any purpose,\n\n\nPardons, quashed convictions and spent convictions  Part VIIC\nPardons for persons wrongly convicted, and quashed convictions  Division 2\n\nSection 85ZU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe fact that the person has been charged with, or convicted\nof, the offence.\n\n(2) Subject to Division 6, but despite any other Commonwealth law or\nany Territory law, where a person’s conviction of a State offence\nor a foreign offence has been quashed, the person is not required:\n\n(a) in any Territory—to disclose to any person, for any purpose,\nthe fact that the person has been charged with, or convicted\nof, the offence; or\n\n(b) in any State or foreign country—to disclose to any\nCommonwealth authority in that State or country, for any\npurpose, the fact that the person has been charged with, or\nconvicted of, the offence.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zt-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zt-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "205493f0c8a200d0f00f3354aa178c3e4a6336707024036b20799cf05c31c968"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "85ZT Quashed convictions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 192,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to Division 6, but despite any other Commonwealth law or\nany State law or Territory law, where a person’s conviction of a\nCommonwealth offence or a Territory offence has been quashed,\nthe person is not required:\n\n(a) in any State or Territory—to disclose to any person, for any\npurpose, the fact that the person has been charged with, or\nconvicted of, the offence; or\n\n(b) in a foreign country—to disclose to any Commonwealth\nauthority or State authority in that country, for any purpose,\n\n\nPardons, quashed convictions and spent convictions  Part VIIC\nPardons for persons wrongly convicted, and quashed convictions  Division 2\n\nSection 85ZU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe fact that the person has been charged with, or convicted\nof, the offence.\n\n(2) Subject to Division 6, but despite any other Commonwealth law or\nany Territory law, where a person’s conviction of a State offence\nor a foreign offence has been quashed, the person is not required:\n\n(a) in any Territory—to disclose to any person, for any purpose,\nthe fact that the person has been charged with, or convicted\nof, the offence; or\n\n(b) in any State or foreign country—to disclose to any\nCommonwealth authority in that State or country, for any\npurpose, the fact that the person has been charged with, or\nconvicted of, the offence."
    },
