    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zz-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "85ZZ(2) Information Commissioner’s functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zz-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a complaint is about an act or practice of another\nCommonwealth authority or State authority, or a member or officer\nof such an authority, being an authority that is within the\nresponsibility of a Commonwealth or State Minister but not within\nthe responsibility of a Commonwealth Department or a State\nDepartment, the Minister is the respondent to the complaint.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If a complaint is about an act or practice of another\nCommonwealth authority or State authority, or a member or officer\nof such an authority, being an authority that is within the\nresponsibility of a Commonwealth or State Minister but not within\nthe responsibility of a Commonwealth Department or a State\nDepartment, the Minister is the respondent to the complaint.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zz"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zz-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zz-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-85zz-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "682271f4d9f39559d8eb83fe38dbdfe52a25bf3cc11808b2584a1706598f9246",
      "skos:note": "Minister is respondent to complaint about act or practice of another authority Ensure protection of human rights and social interests while performing functions. Complaint must be in writing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-85zz-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "85ZZ(2) Information Commissioner’s functions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a complaint is about an act or practice of another\nCommonwealth authority or State authority, or a member or officer\nof such an authority, being an authority that is within the\nresponsibility of a Commonwealth or State Minister but not within\nthe responsibility of a Commonwealth Department or a State\nDepartment, the Minister is the respondent to the complaint."
    },
