    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "89(5) Trespassing on Commonwealth land",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-89-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.224",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\nauthorized Commonwealth officer means a Commonwealth\nofficer declared by a Minister, by instrument in writing, to be an\nauthorized Commonwealth officer for the purposes of this section.\nprohibited Commonwealth land means land belonging to, or in the\noccupation of, the Commonwealth or a public authority under the\nCommonwealth, being land upon which is posted a notice to the\neffect that trespassing upon the land is prohibited.\nprotective service officer has the same meaning as in the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In this section:\nauthorized Commonwealth officer means a Commonwealth\nofficer declared by a Minister, by instrument in writing, to be an\nauthorized Commonwealth officer for the purposes of this section.\nprohibited Commonwealth land means land belonging to, or in the\noccupation of, the Commonwealth or a public authority under the\nCommonwealth, being land upon which is posted a notice to the\neffect that trespassing upon the land is prohibited.\nprotective service officer has the same meaning as in the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a2bca389c87da508dc4e7d6f465c714e98028fa39a83ce77cf1098bf527d407e",
      "skos:note": "Trespassing on prohibited Commonwealth land is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-89-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "89(5) Trespassing on Commonwealth land",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 224,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\nauthorized Commonwealth officer means a Commonwealth\nofficer declared by a Minister, by instrument in writing, to be an\nauthorized Commonwealth officer for the purposes of this section.\nprohibited Commonwealth land means land belonging to, or in the\noccupation of, the Commonwealth or a public authority under the\nCommonwealth, being land upon which is posted a notice to the\neffect that trespassing upon the land is prohibited.\nprotective service officer has the same meaning as in the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979."
    },
