    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "89A Discharging firearms on or over Commonwealth land",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-89a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.225",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who, without lawful authority or excuse (proof whereof\nshall lie upon him or her), discharges a firearm upon or over a\nprohibited area commits an offence and the firearms shall be\nforfeited to the Commonwealth.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n\n(2) A person who commits an offence against this section may be\napprehended by a constable or an authorized Commonwealth\nofficer and detained in proper custody to be dealt with according to\nlaw.\n\n(3) An authorized Commonwealth officer shall not, under this section,\napprehend a person unless he or she first produces to the person the\ninstrument by virtue of which he or she is an authorized\nCommonwealth officer.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who, without lawful authority or excuse (proof whereof\nshall lie upon him or her), discharges a firearm upon or over a\nprohibited area commits an offence and the firearms shall be\nforfeited to the Commonwealth.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n\n(2) A person who commits an offence against this section may be\napprehended by a constable or an authorized Commonwealth\nofficer and detained in proper custody to be dealt with according to\nlaw.\n\n(3) An authorized Commonwealth officer shall not, under this section,\napprehend a person unless he or she first produces to the person the\ninstrument by virtue of which he or she is an authorized\nCommonwealth officer.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-89a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7ce9021a099409c77a4fb533503d67a040f77b28c20b8d8081ad297788ef4dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-89a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "89A Discharging firearms on or over Commonwealth land",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 225,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who, without lawful authority or excuse (proof whereof\nshall lie upon him or her), discharges a firearm upon or over a\nprohibited area commits an offence and the firearms shall be\nforfeited to the Commonwealth.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 6 months.\n\n(2) A person who commits an offence against this section may be\napprehended by a constable or an authorized Commonwealth\nofficer and detained in proper custody to be dealt with according to\nlaw.\n\n(3) An authorized Commonwealth officer shall not, under this section,\napprehend a person unless he or she first produces to the person the\ninstrument by virtue of which he or she is an authorized\nCommonwealth officer."
    },
